WEBVTT

1
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.571
KING: <i>I accept this honor
for our lost ones,</i>

2
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.166
<i>whose deaths pave our path.</i>

3
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.407
And for the 20 million
Negro men and women

4
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.608
motivated by dignity

5
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.762
and a disdain for hopelessness.

6
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.121
This isn't right.

7
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.440
Corrie.

8
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.051
This ain't right.

9
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.326
CORETTA: What's that?

10
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.486
This necktie. It's not right.

11
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.604
Well, it's not a necktie, dear.

12
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.761
It's an ascot.

13
00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.890
Yes, but generally the same principles
should apply, shouldn't they?

14
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.211
It's not right.

15
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.689
It's not right, or you don't like it?

16
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.921
(SIGHS) I don't like how this looks.

17
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.606
Looks distinguished and debonair to me.

18
00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.126
You know what I mean.

19
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.204
Like we're living high on the hog.

20
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.127
Dressed like this
while folks back home are... (SIGHS)

21
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.043
It's not right.

22
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.369
Wait till the brothers
back home see me like this.

23
00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.805
They'll have a good laugh.

24
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.167
Let them laugh.

25
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.767
It's not a crime to be away
for a few days, Martin.

26
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.648
It's nice being away, huh?

27
00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.245
Yeah. It really is.

28
00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:16.881
Look here.

29
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:21.531
I'm gonna be a pastor somewhere small.

30
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.165
College town.

31
00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.765
(CHUCKLING)

32
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.606
Lead a little church. Teach a class.

33
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.447
(SIGHS)

34
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.683
Maybe the occasional
speaking engagement.

35
00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.410
And I'll pay all the bills for us,

36
00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.689
especially the mortgage
for our very own house.

37
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.611
Perfect.

38
00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.765
You look handsome.

39
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.923
JAHN: <i>Through it all,</i>

40
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.562
Martin Luther King
has spoken of his dream.

41
00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.404
One which we

42
00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.371
and many other people
around the world share.

43
00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.603
To this undeterred hero for justice,

44
00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.081
the Nobel Committee of Oslo, Norway,

45
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.564
awards our 1964 Peace Prize.

46
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.483
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

47
00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.806
KING: <i>I accept this honor
for our lost ones,</i>

48
00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.009
<i>whose deaths pave our path.</i>

49
00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.690
<i>I accept this honor for</i>

50
00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.287
<i>the more than 20 million
American Negroes</i>

51
00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.409
<i>who are motivated by dignity.</i>

52
00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.087
<i>Together we believe that
what the illusion</i>

53
00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.481
<i>of supremacy has destroyed,</i>

54
00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.084
<i>the truth of equality can nourish.</i>

55
00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.561
GIRL 1: I promise you.
It ain't nothing to be scared of.

56
00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.722
It's quick. And the pastor
is right there next to you.

57
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.280
GIRL 2: Yeah, but the biggest thing
is getting your hair wet up.

58
00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.771
I got my hair pressed that same morning

59
00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.922
and it was wasted
as soon as I hit the water.

60
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.604
I should have worn
a swim cap like Mama said.

61
00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:27.886
(CHILDREN LAUGHING)

62
00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.246
GIRL 3: See, I asked my mama

63
00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.800
could she make my hair like
Coretta Scott King had hers

64
00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:33.450
at the Washington March.

65
00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.170
But she said that was too grown.

66
00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.605
Oh, I love her hair.

67
00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:39.365
I heard she don't even put rollers in it.
It's just like that.

68
00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.761
But I studied it. I know how she do it.

69
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.002
See, she parts in the middle and then...

70
00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.167
(SIGHS)

71
00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.681
MAN: Annie Lee Cooper!

72
00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.000
(SIGHS)

73
00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:50.687
Get on up now. I ain't got all day.

74
00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.601
You work for Mr. Dunn
down at the rest home, ain't that right?

75
00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.486
Yes.

76
00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.810
Wonder what old Dunn'll say
when I tell him

77
00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:16.770
one of his gals is down here
stirring a fuss.

78
00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.444
I ain't stirring no fuss.

79
00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:20.727
I'm just here trying to register to vote.

80
00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:26.965
It's all right this time.

81
00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.804
It's right when I say it's right.

82
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.446
Recite the Constitution's preamble.

83
00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.567
Know what a preamble is?

84
00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:48.571
"We the people of the United States,

85
00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.691
"in order to form a more perfect union,

86
00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.971
"establish justice,

87
00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:00.121
"ensure domestic tranquility,

88
00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.005
"provide for the common defense,

89
00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.366
"promote the general welfare..."

90
00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:08.284
How many county judges in Alabama?

91
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.082
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

92
00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.524
Sixty-seven.

93
00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.410
Name them.

94
00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.245
JOHNSON: <i>Aren't we done?</i>

95
00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.685
<i>Are we not done with this?</i>

96
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:51.767
Will this ever end?

97
00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.046
I don't know, Mr. President.

98
00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.122
A comprehensive plan
is already in place.

99
00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.885
The act was only passed six months ago.

100
00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:01.885
So hammer home that impatience
only hurts the overall cause.

101
00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.564
We're... We're getting there.

102
00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.324
Just... Just keep reiterating the plan.

103
00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:06.726
No, he doesn't want reiteration.

104
00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.290
He wants something so he can say,

105
00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.402
"Look, I told you I had a dream

106
00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.845
"and it's all coming goddamn true,

107
00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:14.571
"whether you like it or not!"
That's what he wants.

108
00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.961
What he needs to do
is get on board with what we're doing

109
00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.202
instead of the other way around.
For once!

110
00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.082
Mr. President, Dr. King.

111
00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.040
KING: Mr. President.

112
00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:26.720
Dr. King.

113
00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.325
(CHUCKLES)

114
00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.846
Well, I'll tell you.
I'm a tall son-of-a-bitch,

115
00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.003
but this close to the new Nobel laureate

116
00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:36.765
and with all those other trinkets
you've been collecting lately,

117
00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.569
I feel tits-high to a puppy dog.

118
00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.685
Well, thank you, Mr. President.

119
00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.681
Mr. White.

120
00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.046
- Dr. King.
- All right.

121
00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.602
I'll tell you, ending segregation,

122
00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:50.968
proudest moment of my life
when I signed that '64 Act.

123
00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.685
Proudest moment of my life, I tell you.

124
00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.285
Now civil rights is a priority

125
00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.761
- of this administration as you know.
- Thank you.

126
00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.001
We're gonna face the challenge,

127
00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.442
or this country is
storing up a heap of trouble for itself.

128
00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:06.126
Now, seeing as I can't convince you to

129
00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.565
work with my administration

130
00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.167
in an official capacity
inside the White House,

131
00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:12.605
I feel damn fortunate

132
00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.250
to have someone
as statesmanlike as you

133
00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.446
leading the movement.

134
00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:17.443
And I want you to go on leading it.
No one else.

135
00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.569
Not one of these
militant Malcolm X types.

136
00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.205
(JOHNSON CHUCKLING)

137
00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:25.727
So... I wanna help. Tell me how.

138
00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.449
Well, Mr. President,

139
00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:33.411
I'm here to speak
specifically about the denial

140
00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.882
of a basic American right
for the Negro citizen.

141
00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.243
The right to vote.

142
00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.482
Well, uh... Technically...

143
00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:46.040
Technically, we already have it.

144
00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.485
Yes, Mr. President.

145
00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.643
But, we both know in the South

146
00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:53.121
black voters are kept off the rolls

147
00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:54.486
and out of the voting booths

148
00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:59.088
by systematic intimidation
and fear, Mr. President.

149
00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:02.884
(CLEARS THROAT) Now,
you asked how you can help.

150
00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.560
We want Federal legislation

151
00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:10.531
granting Negroes the right
to vote unencumbered.

152
00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:14.002
And we want Federal
protocol eliminating

153
00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:16.651
the decades-long dismissal

154
00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:20.088
and illegal denial of
blacks seeking to vote.

155
00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:24.000
And we want
robust enforcement of that protocol.

156
00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.050
Well, um... (CLEARS THROAT)
That's fine.

157
00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.569
But... Most of the South
is still not desegregating.

158
00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.611
Let's not start another battle
when we haven't even won the first.

159
00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.523
And you know what
the next battle should be?

160
00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.126
The eradication of poverty.

161
00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.643
I'm calling it "The War on Poverty."

162
00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.649
It's a matter of political priorities.

163
00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:56.805
Poverty is going to be my focus at home
and I want you to help me with this.

164
00:11:57.640 --> 00:11:59.802
We can make big changes
in these things

165
00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.530
for people of all colors.

166
00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.921
And I know that matters to you,
doesn't it?

167
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.241
This voting thing
is just gonna have to wait.

168
00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:09.845
(CLEARING THROAT)

169
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.365
It...

170
00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.569
(STAMMERING)
It can't wait, Mr. President.

171
00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:18.641
Well, why not?

172
00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:20.927
Because there have been thousands

173
00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.401
of racially motivated murders
in the South,

174
00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:25.926
including those four girls.

175
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.081
Well, I know that...

176
00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:32.200
And you know the astounding fact
that not one of these criminals

177
00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:34.681
who murder us when and why they want

178
00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:36.410
has ever been convicted.

179
00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.164
Yeah, I know we have a lot
of work to do down there.

180
00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.924
Not one conviction

181
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:43.004
because they are protected
by white officials

182
00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.606
chosen by an all-white electorate.

183
00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:48.524
And on the rare occasions
that they face trial,

184
00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:51.604
they are freed by all-white juries.

185
00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.720
All-white because
you can't serve on a jury

186
00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:59.371
unless you are registered to vote.

187
00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:07.169
Well, Dr. King, you've certainly given me
something to think about.

188
00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:10.926
But this administration is going
to set this aside for a while.

189
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.367
Just for a while, you understand.

190
00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:20.203
Yes, Mr. President, I... I understand.

191
00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.243
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

192
00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:31.130
Selma it is.

193
00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:48.684
Big speech lined up
for these folks tonight, Doc?

194
00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:53.326
We need to see
what's what first, Big Fellow.

195
00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:55.801
We're just here to test the waters.

196
00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:59.248
Oh, my Lord.
What you got us into, woman?

197
00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:03.406
We've got 128 miles

198
00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.642
to come to our senses, gentlemen.

199
00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.006
NASH: Hush.

200
00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:09.765
This here is the place we need to be.

201
00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:12.491
This right here is the next great battle.

202
00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.328
I can only imagine.

203
00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:17.281
Hmm.

204
00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.649
Decent-looking place to die though.

205
00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:23.324
(ABERNATHY CHUCKLES WRYLY)

206
00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:47.847
Ms. Nash.

207
00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.446
Mr. Bevel.

208
00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:53.889
Doc? This here is it. Selma's the place.

209
00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.491
A lot of groundwork
has already been laid

210
00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.050
by the people here.

211
00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.167
And they ready.

212
00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.808
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

213
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.001
(DOOR OPENS)

214
00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.204
ORANGE: Sister Boynton.
BOYNTON: Mr. Orange.

215
00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:29.126
Good afternoon.

216
00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:36.808
MAN 1: Dr. King?

217
00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:39.368
May I introduce myself?

218
00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:42.129
Yeah, of course.

219
00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:44.886
- (GROANS)
- MAN 2: Hey!

220
00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.371
(PEOPLE CLAMORING)

221
00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.331
It's okay. It's okay. I'm okay.

222
00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:54.446
This way, Dr. King.

223
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.688
KING: That white boy can hit.

224
00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.683
ABERNATHY: This place is perfect.

225
00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.604
What's the FBI's current information
on Martin Luther King?

226
00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.646
I heard he was assaulted in Selma.

227
00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:13.611
My information can be
summed up in a few words.

228
00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:17.810
King is a political and moral degenerate.

229
00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.646
Well, you say that, J. Edgar.
I have to take it seriously.

230
00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.849
But if he's a degenerate,
what I do know is,

231
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.122
he's a non-violent degenerate.

232
00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.124
And I want him to go on leading
the civil rights movement,

233
00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.521
not one of these bloodthirsty militants.

234
00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:37.205
What I need to know right now is
what's he about to do next?

235
00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:39.611
Mr. President,

236
00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:45.129
you know we can shut men
with power down

237
00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:49.091
permanently and unequivocally.

238
00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:55.689
I'm very aware of that, Mr. Director.

239
00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:04.811
Well, if you prefer a different approach,

240
00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.450
we can go with the wife.

241
00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:15.570
We know there's tension
in the home already.

242
00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:20.762
We can weaken the dynamic.

243
00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.324
Dismantle the family.

244
00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.403
(CHILDREN LAUGHING)

245
00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.450
(PHONE RINGING)

246
00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:56.761
Hello.

247
00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.808
MAN: (ON PHONE) <i>You ain't got long.</i>

248
00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:02.927
<i>When the hearts of those Pickaninnies
of yours stop beating...</i>

249
00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.010
Same thing?

250
00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.526
CORETTA: When are
you all heading out?

251
00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:18.806
KING: We're heading back
to Selma at 5:00 a.m.

252
00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:22.043
It turned out to be
an ideal staging ground.

253
00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:28.202
There's a full couple of weeks planned.

254
00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.130
Quite a bit to be done.

255
00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:36.845
I see.

256
00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:44.169
That highway is nice now.

257
00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.368
Get you there in a couple of hours.

258
00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.091
Good people in those parts though.

259
00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:06.561
Well...

260
00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.925
I'm worried about the ones
who ain't so good.

261
00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.531
This local Sheriff Jim Clark

262
00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:18.887
is supposed to be bad business.

263
00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.562
Won't go down without a fight, they say.

264
00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:27.402
And since we don't fight...

265
00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.121
Well...

266
00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.841
As good a place to die as any, I guess.

267
00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:38.608
I wish you wouldn't talk like that.

268
00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.322
It just takes the edge off.

269
00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.523
You and your friends can joke about that.

270
00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:51.443
I don't joke about that.

271
00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.524
You're right. I'm sorry.

272
00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.243
I'll, uh, put these things
away in your bag now.

273
00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:06.846
I didn't realize you were leaving so early.

274
00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.651
(SIGHS)

275
00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.484
(PHONE RINGING)

276
00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.930
Hello?

277
00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.126
KING: (ON PHONE) <i>Halie?</i>

278
00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.570
<i>Martin.</i>

279
00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:03.882
I need to hear the Lord's voice.

280
00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:06.966
Oh.

281
00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.482
Surely, Martin. Surely.

282
00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.050
(JACKSON CLEARS THROAT)

283
00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:28.969
JACKSON: (SINGING) <i>Precious Lord</i>

284
00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:34.169
<i>Take my hand</i>

285
00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:42.205
<i>Lead me home</i>

286
00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:47.721
<i>Let me stand</i>

287
00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:53.326
<i>I am tired</i>

288
00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:55.370
(KING SIGHS)

289
00:21:56.760 --> 00:22:01.402
<i>I am weak</i>

290
00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:09.569
<i>I am worn</i>

291
00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:19.285
<i>Through the storm</i>

292
00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:26.883
<i>Through the night</i>

293
00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:36.644
<i>Lord, lead me on</i>

294
00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:39.481
<i>To the light</i>

295
00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:41.803
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

296
00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:43.964
- KING: Hey!
- Hey!

297
00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:45.530
- Sully.
- Look at you.

298
00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:46.601
(LAUGHING)

299
00:22:46.680 --> 00:22:49.047
- Morning, Doctor.
- Good morning, Doctor.

300
00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:50.360
SULLIVAN: Drive all right?

301
00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:51.726
KING: Good and long.

302
00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:54.644
Good news is Richie Jean is in there.

303
00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:56.324
Oh, she's ready for you.

304
00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:57.731
(ALL LAUGHING)

305
00:22:57.800 --> 00:23:00.280
Negro, that's all you had to say.

306
00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:03.244
Uncle Marty!

307
00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.601
There she is! There's our girl!

308
00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:08.050
Hey, Richie Jean!

309
00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:09.804
RICHIE JEAN: Oh!

310
00:23:10.440 --> 00:23:12.249
- KING: Looking like her mom.
- You go play.

311
00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.368
- Hey!
- Hey, Ralphy.

312
00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:17.605
ABERNATHY: How you doing?
RICHIE JEAN: Hey!

313
00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:20.246
- Good to see you, sweetheart.
- Hey, come over here.

314
00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.445
ABERNATHY: Oh, Lord,
it's good to see this!

315
00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:25.602
Okay, now, I've got the grits on the stove.

316
00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:27.648
Uh, how many we expecting today?

317
00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:30.001
Well, now, Sister Jackson.

318
00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:32.686
You know about our group,
the SCLC, right?

319
00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:34.728
The Southern Christian
Leadership Conference?

320
00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:37.246
A few of our top SCLC leaders
are with us this time

321
00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:40.767
since we're going to
be here a little longer than expected.

322
00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:42.850
Now, this here's Reverend C.T. Vivian.

323
00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:44.649
He coordinates all the SCLC branches.

324
00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:47.405
Welcome. Nice to meet you.
Welcome, welcome.

325
00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:49.323
This is Reverend James Bevel.

326
00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:51.448
- How you doing, ma'am?
- I'm well. Thank you.

327
00:23:51.520 --> 00:23:53.090
YOUNG: This here is James Orange.

328
00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:54.565
Oh, this is a big one.

329
00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:56.130
I don't know if I've got
enough to feed you.

330
00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.690
Well, let's find out. How about that?

331
00:23:57.760 --> 00:23:58.807
- RICHIE JEAN: Hey!
- (ALL LAUGHING)

332
00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.008
Now, you got two of them named James.

333
00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:02.241
Oh, you can call me Jim, Sister.

334
00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:03.446
And Orange is fine with me, ma'am.

335
00:24:03.520 --> 00:24:04.760
Or Big Fellow!

336
00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:06.769
All right. Well, this is fine with me.

337
00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:09.963
Mrs. Jackson. Hosea Williams.

338
00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:11.280
Or Castro!

339
00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:13.328
Oh, yeah, that's a long story.

340
00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:17.166
Uh, those grits, they need
some stirring. Mind?

341
00:24:17.240 --> 00:24:18.844
ABERNATHY: You put
your foot in it now.

342
00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:20.968
Ain't you supposed to be on a diet?

343
00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:22.201
(ALL LAUGHING)

344
00:24:22.280 --> 00:24:23.441
Somebody call Juanita.

345
00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:25.761
- There's a phone!
- Hey, get off that phone.

346
00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:27.927
Juanita?

347
00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.207
ABERNATHY: <i>Don't do it, Doc.
Don't do it...</i>

348
00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:33.050
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

349
00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:36.049
Turning in, Doc. You okay?

350
00:24:36.960 --> 00:24:39.531
Yes, sir. Good night to you.

351
00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.885
Uh...

352
00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:47.243
I wanted to tell you that
the students are in town.

353
00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:51.160
Local students?

354
00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:52.969
Oh, no.

355
00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:57.080
The Student Non-Violent
Coordinating Committee.

356
00:24:57.160 --> 00:25:02.963
- Oh. Okay. Our young friends at SNCC.
- Mmm-hmm.

357
00:25:03.600 --> 00:25:05.011
Good to know.

358
00:25:05.080 --> 00:25:06.969
You the one told them to organize.

359
00:25:08.480 --> 00:25:09.481
Took it to heart.

360
00:25:10.200 --> 00:25:13.488
Don't be surprised
if they don't give us grief tomorrow.

361
00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:16.245
Town folk may be happy
to see us. But SNCC?

362
00:25:16.600 --> 00:25:18.762
They feel we're in their territory.

363
00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:23.927
- They're young and full of spirit.
- Mmm.

364
00:25:24.040 --> 00:25:25.371
Not a bad thing.

365
00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:29.209
It'll sort out.

366
00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:33.330
Good night.

367
00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:36.965
Good night.

368
00:25:40.680 --> 00:25:45.049
"Boycotting the buses in Montgomery.

369
00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:47.282
- "Segregation in Birmingham."
- (APPLAUSE)

370
00:25:48.720 --> 00:25:50.484
<i>Boycotting the buses in Montgomery.</i>

371
00:25:53.800 --> 00:25:56.610
<i>Segregation in Birmingham.</i>

372
00:25:56.680 --> 00:25:58.091
(AUDIENCE AGREEING)

373
00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:01.966
<i>Now? Voting in Selma.</i>

374
00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:08.089
<i>One struggle ends just to go
right to the next and the next.</i>

375
00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:13.084
<i>If you think of it that way,
it's a hard road.</i>

376
00:26:14.680 --> 00:26:17.411
<i>But I don't think of it that way.</i>

377
00:26:17.480 --> 00:26:20.245
<i>I think of these efforts as one effort.</i>

378
00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:23.085
<i>And that one effort is for our life.</i>

379
00:26:23.160 --> 00:26:24.889
(AUDIENCE AGREEING)

380
00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:29.568
<i>Our life as a community.
Our life as a nation.</i>

381
00:26:30.200 --> 00:26:32.168
<i>For our lives.</i>

382
00:26:37.520 --> 00:26:38.521
<i>We can do this.</i>

383
00:26:38.600 --> 00:26:39.681
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

384
00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:43.165
<i>We must do this!</i>

385
00:26:45.480 --> 00:26:49.007
<i>We see children</i>

386
00:26:49.080 --> 00:26:51.811
<i>become victims of one
of the most vicious crimes</i>

387
00:26:51.920 --> 00:26:54.082
<i>ever perpetrated against humanity</i>

388
00:26:54.160 --> 00:26:56.208
<i>within the walls of their own church!</i>

389
00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:01.370
<i>They are sainted now.</i>

390
00:27:01.440 --> 00:27:04.762
<i>They are the sainted ones
in this quest for freedom.</i>

391
00:27:04.840 --> 00:27:07.525
<i>And they speak to us still.</i>

392
00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:09.090
<i>They say to us,</i>

393
00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:11.766
<i>to all of us, all colors and creeds,</i>

394
00:27:13.080 --> 00:27:14.730
<i>that we must do this.</i>

395
00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:20.127
<i>They say to us that it is unacceptable</i>

396
00:27:20.240 --> 00:27:23.642
<i>for more than 50% of Selma to be Negro</i>

397
00:27:23.720 --> 00:27:27.202
<i>and yet less than 2% of Negroes here
being able to vote</i>

398
00:27:27.280 --> 00:27:30.284
<i>and determine their own destiny
as human beings.</i>

399
00:27:33.360 --> 00:27:37.490
<i>They say to us that
the local white leadership</i>

400
00:27:37.560 --> 00:27:38.925
<i>use their power</i>

401
00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:42.721
<i>to keep us away from the ballot box
and keep us voiceless.</i>

402
00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:44.211
(APPLAUSE AND AGREEMENT
CONTINUE)

403
00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:50.168
<i>As long as I am unable to exercise
my constitutional right to vote,</i>

404
00:27:50.240 --> 00:27:53.210
<i>I do not have command of my own life.</i>

405
00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:56.807
<i>I cannot determine my own destiny
for it is determined for me</i>

406
00:27:56.880 --> 00:28:00.043
<i>by people who would rather
see me suffer than succeed.</i>

407
00:28:00.920 --> 00:28:04.288
<i>Those that have gone before us say,
"No more!"</i>

408
00:28:04.360 --> 00:28:05.600
AUDIENCE: No more! No more!

409
00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:07.250
<i>No more!</i>

410
00:28:07.320 --> 00:28:11.120
<i>That means protest, that means march,</i>

411
00:28:11.200 --> 00:28:15.444
<i>that means disturb the peace,
that means jail,</i>

412
00:28:15.520 --> 00:28:17.887
<i>that means risk! And that is hard!</i>

413
00:28:17.960 --> 00:28:19.689
(SHOUTS OF AGREEMENT)

414
00:28:20.440 --> 00:28:23.046
<i>We will not wait any longer.</i>

415
00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:25.122
<i>Give us the vote!</i>

416
00:28:25.200 --> 00:28:26.770
That's right! No more!

417
00:28:27.160 --> 00:28:29.367
<i>We're not asking. We're demanding.</i>

418
00:28:29.440 --> 00:28:30.601
<i>Give us the vote!</i>

419
00:28:30.680 --> 00:28:31.806
ALL: Give us the vote!

420
00:28:41.720 --> 00:28:45.441
Dr. King.
Roy Reed of <i>The New York Times.</i>

421
00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:47.522
Yes. Hello to you. How are you?

422
00:28:47.600 --> 00:28:49.921
I'm well, sir. Thank you for asking.

423
00:28:50.040 --> 00:28:54.841
Dr. King, are you truly non-violent
if you are provoking violence, sir?

424
00:28:54.960 --> 00:28:57.964
We are here, using
our very bodies in protest

425
00:28:58.040 --> 00:28:59.883
- to say to those who deny us...
- Dr. King. Dr. King.

426
00:28:59.960 --> 00:29:00.961
Pleasure, sir.

427
00:29:01.040 --> 00:29:03.805
...that we will no longer let them use
their billy clubs

428
00:29:03.880 --> 00:29:06.724
in dark corners and halls of power.

429
00:29:06.800 --> 00:29:09.565
We make them do it
in the glaring light of day, Mr. Reed.

430
00:29:09.640 --> 00:29:11.608
Is SNCC standing with us
on this or not, gentlemen?

431
00:29:11.680 --> 00:29:12.806
You want us to bring our people in,

432
00:29:12.880 --> 00:29:14.086
but you're not giving anything in return.

433
00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:16.606
Now we are asking for
some kind of commitment here.

434
00:29:16.680 --> 00:29:18.603
Respectfully speaking, of course,

435
00:29:18.680 --> 00:29:21.047
we've been handling
the voter registration

436
00:29:21.120 --> 00:29:22.531
in this town now for two years.

437
00:29:22.600 --> 00:29:25.001
Well, you haven't gotten
very far, have you?

438
00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:28.766
Well, maybe not, Reverend.
But we're still here.

439
00:29:28.840 --> 00:29:29.921
WILLIAMS: Meaning what?

440
00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:31.525
FORMAN: This time next month,
you won't be!

441
00:29:31.600 --> 00:29:33.682
- WILLIAMS: That's insanity!
- Just like you left Albany.

442
00:29:33.760 --> 00:29:35.205
Those people are pathetic
down there now.

443
00:29:35.280 --> 00:29:36.441
Like they daddy left home!

444
00:29:36.520 --> 00:29:38.648
What we're trying to explain
is that in Albany you all...

445
00:29:38.720 --> 00:29:41.564
You know what I think?
Maybe we should just leave Selma...

446
00:29:41.640 --> 00:29:42.607
Now!

447
00:29:42.680 --> 00:29:43.681
Leave it to these two.

448
00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:46.041
Come back in another two years
and see how much further you got!

449
00:29:46.120 --> 00:29:47.929
- Sounds just fine to me.
- KING: That's enough.

450
00:29:50.040 --> 00:29:51.041
Enough of this now.

451
00:29:54.040 --> 00:29:55.121
I haven't the time for this.

452
00:29:55.200 --> 00:29:56.725
None of us got the time for this.

453
00:29:59.400 --> 00:30:00.686
John.

454
00:30:01.600 --> 00:30:02.931
James.

455
00:30:04.040 --> 00:30:07.681
The way our organization works
is straightforward.

456
00:30:07.760 --> 00:30:11.970
We negotiate. We demonstrate.
We resist.

457
00:30:12.440 --> 00:30:17.048
And on our best days, our adversary
helps the matter by making a mistake.

458
00:30:17.720 --> 00:30:22.169
Now, we were in Albany for nine months
and we made a lot of mistakes.

459
00:30:22.720 --> 00:30:25.326
But their sheriff, Laurie Pritchett,

460
00:30:25.920 --> 00:30:27.570
he never made a mistake.

461
00:30:27.640 --> 00:30:31.042
Kept his cool,
kept arresting us in a humane way,

462
00:30:31.120 --> 00:30:34.567
carried people to
the jail-wagons on stretchers.

463
00:30:34.640 --> 00:30:36.768
Day in, day out.

464
00:30:37.400 --> 00:30:39.846
- There was no drama.
- You mean there was no cameras.

465
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.001
Exactly.

466
00:30:45.440 --> 00:30:48.364
Now I know, we all understand,
that you young people

467
00:30:48.440 --> 00:30:51.205
believe in working in
the community long-term.

468
00:30:51.280 --> 00:30:55.126
Doing the good work
to raise black consciousness.

469
00:30:57.040 --> 00:30:58.883
It's good grassroots work.

470
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.971
I can't tell you how much we admire that.

471
00:31:04.360 --> 00:31:06.328
But what we do

472
00:31:06.400 --> 00:31:08.368
is negotiate,

473
00:31:08.440 --> 00:31:09.965
demonstrate,

474
00:31:10.040 --> 00:31:11.121
resist.

475
00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:13.288
And a big part of that

476
00:31:13.360 --> 00:31:16.443
is raising white consciousness.

477
00:31:16.560 --> 00:31:18.050
And in particular the consciousness

478
00:31:18.120 --> 00:31:20.805
of whichever white man happens
to be sitting in the Oval Office.

479
00:31:21.640 --> 00:31:25.929
Right now, Johnson has other fish to fry
and he'll ignore us if he can.

480
00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:29.771
The only way to stop him doing that

481
00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:32.571
is by being on the front page
of the national press every morning

482
00:31:33.240 --> 00:31:36.961
and by being on the TV news every night.

483
00:31:37.080 --> 00:31:39.162
And that requires

484
00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:41.161
drama.

485
00:31:42.640 --> 00:31:43.801
Now...

486
00:31:46.320 --> 00:31:47.526
John.

487
00:31:49.720 --> 00:31:51.085
James.

488
00:31:51.160 --> 00:31:52.889
Answer me one question.

489
00:31:54.160 --> 00:31:58.882
I've been told the sheriff in this town
isn't like Laurie Pritchett in Albany.

490
00:31:58.960 --> 00:32:03.249
He's a big ignorant bully
like Bull Connor in Birmingham.

491
00:32:04.480 --> 00:32:07.643
Well, you tell me. You know Selma.

492
00:32:07.720 --> 00:32:10.166
You know Sheriff Jim Clark.

493
00:32:10.840 --> 00:32:13.207
Is he Laurie Pritchett?

494
00:32:13.280 --> 00:32:15.521
Or is he Bull Connor?

495
00:32:25.120 --> 00:32:26.121
He's Bull Connor.

496
00:32:27.040 --> 00:32:28.849
- ABERNATHY: Bingo!
- Good.

497
00:32:31.200 --> 00:32:32.531
That's good.

498
00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:36.721
But it gets better.

499
00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:41.251
<i>See, Clark doesn't control the streets
like Connor did in Birmingham.</i>

500
00:32:41.320 --> 00:32:42.560
<i>Clark's the County Sheriff,</i>

501
00:32:42.640 --> 00:32:45.803
<i>and all he controls in Selma
is the County Courthouse.</i>

502
00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:47.245
<i>So relatively speaking,</i>

503
00:32:47.360 --> 00:32:49.806
<i>we have clear avenues of approach</i>

504
00:32:49.880 --> 00:32:52.121
<i>to a defined battle zone.</i>

505
00:32:52.240 --> 00:32:53.730
(MUSIC PLAYING)

506
00:33:46.960 --> 00:33:50.203
<i>In the courthouse sits
the heart of the matter,</i>

507
00:33:50.280 --> 00:33:52.567
<i>the voter registration office.</i>

508
00:33:52.640 --> 00:33:54.529
<i>Now this is an exceptional circumstance.</i>

509
00:33:54.600 --> 00:33:58.650
<i>See, in Albany, there were
no clearly defined battle zones.</i>

510
00:33:58.720 --> 00:34:00.643
<i>The issue was segregation,</i>

511
00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:03.041
<i>and segregation was everywhere.</i>

512
00:34:03.120 --> 00:34:08.126
<i>In Selma, we can concentrate
our actions on one building.</i>

513
00:34:08.560 --> 00:34:10.847
<i>A citadel, defended by fanatics.</i>

514
00:34:11.960 --> 00:34:13.450
<i>The Selma Courthouse.</i>

515
00:34:14.640 --> 00:34:16.369
<i>A perfect stage.</i>

516
00:34:18.320 --> 00:34:20.800
(WHITE PEOPLE
SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

517
00:34:31.880 --> 00:34:34.326
CLARK: Y'all deliberately
causing an obstruction!

518
00:34:35.640 --> 00:34:37.847
You don't disperse,
you're gonna be arrested.

519
00:34:37.920 --> 00:34:39.046
I promise you!

520
00:34:39.120 --> 00:34:40.804
Sheriff Clark,

521
00:34:40.880 --> 00:34:43.724
we're trying to gain access
to the registration office.

522
00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:45.404
Which is our legal right.

523
00:34:45.520 --> 00:34:46.646
CLARK: There's too many of you.

524
00:34:46.720 --> 00:34:48.085
And you know damn well there is!

525
00:34:48.160 --> 00:34:50.288
Now, y'all just gonna have
to wait at the rear!

526
00:34:50.400 --> 00:34:51.925
No, Sheriff Clark.

527
00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:53.411
We're going in the front

528
00:34:53.480 --> 00:34:55.482
and we're gonna wait right here.

529
00:34:55.560 --> 00:34:58.882
Segregation is now illegal
in this country, sir.

530
00:34:58.960 --> 00:35:00.849
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING CONTINUES)

531
00:35:01.440 --> 00:35:02.521
WOMAN: Get out, nigger.

532
00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:03.647
JIMMIE: Come on.
CAGER: I'm trying.

533
00:35:03.720 --> 00:35:04.801
VIOLA: Kneel down, Daddy.

534
00:35:05.840 --> 00:35:06.921
CLARK: Come on.

535
00:35:07.440 --> 00:35:09.283
Keep this sidewalk clear. Clear a path!

536
00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:12.125
Get out of the way! Get out of the way!

537
00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:13.611
Get the hell out of the way!

538
00:35:13.680 --> 00:35:15.250
Keep the sidewalk clear!

539
00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:17.041
I said keep it clear!

540
00:35:17.120 --> 00:35:18.610
Okay. We about to sit him down.
He can't sit.

541
00:35:18.720 --> 00:35:19.801
CLARK: Then he needs to learn.

542
00:35:19.880 --> 00:35:21.644
- He gonna sit.
- Sit down, God damn it!

543
00:35:21.720 --> 00:35:23.449
JIMMIE: Hey, hey! Pa? Pa?

544
00:35:23.880 --> 00:35:25.245
VIOLA: Daddy.

545
00:35:26.880 --> 00:35:28.564
JIMMIE: I just told you he can't sit.

546
00:35:28.640 --> 00:35:30.051
CLARK: Oh, what do we got here?

547
00:35:31.080 --> 00:35:32.127
What's going on here, boy?

548
00:35:32.200 --> 00:35:33.486
What we got here? What we got here?

549
00:35:33.560 --> 00:35:35.369
- Jimmie! Sit down!
- No, Mama, I'm sick of this.

550
00:35:35.440 --> 00:35:36.566
- Jimmie!
- VIOLA: Don't do it.

551
00:35:36.640 --> 00:35:37.641
Do you have a problem, boy?

552
00:35:37.720 --> 00:35:39.324
JIMMIE: I'm sick of this! I just told you...

553
00:35:39.400 --> 00:35:41.801
CLARK: What'd you think, boy?
What'd you think?

554
00:35:41.880 --> 00:35:43.484
What the fuck are you thinking?

555
00:35:43.560 --> 00:35:44.721
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

556
00:35:47.640 --> 00:35:48.721
(BOTH GRUNTING)

557
00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:50.040
(PEOPLE GASP)

558
00:35:54.240 --> 00:35:55.480
Get that nigger woman!

559
00:35:55.560 --> 00:35:56.721
MAN: Kill that nigger bitch!

560
00:35:57.440 --> 00:35:58.646
Get your hands off of me!

561
00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:02.129
- (GRUNTING)
- (PEOPLE CLAMORING)

562
00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:03.961
(SCREAMING INDISTINCTLY)

563
00:36:14.520 --> 00:36:17.922
WALLACE: <i>We will not tolerate
a bunch of nigra agitators</i>

564
00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:21.686
<i>attempting to orchestrate
a disturbance in this state.</i>

565
00:36:21.760 --> 00:36:23.603
<i>Not as long as I'm governor.</i>

566
00:36:28.200 --> 00:36:29.247
<i>Now, I stand here today</i>

567
00:36:29.320 --> 00:36:30.321
(CAMERA CLICKING)

568
00:36:30.400 --> 00:36:32.323
<i>in the cradle of the Confederacy</i>

569
00:36:32.400 --> 00:36:37.042
<i>to remind its people
of our Founding Fathers' goals of duty.</i>

570
00:36:37.120 --> 00:36:40.329
<i>Goals long since forgotten
by progressives and liberals</i>

571
00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:43.927
<i>in favor of what they call
a changing world.</i>

572
00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:47.846
<i>They seek to make us one mongrel unit.</i>

573
00:36:47.920 --> 00:36:52.050
<i>Instead of allowing each race to flourish
from its separate racial station</i>

574
00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:54.521
<i>as has been the standard
for generations now.</i>

575
00:36:54.600 --> 00:36:55.726
Good morning, Mr. President.

576
00:36:55.800 --> 00:36:57.802
<i>Their changing world</i>

577
00:36:57.880 --> 00:36:59.848
<i>is sickening the balance
of the Southland.</i>

578
00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:03.086
<i>Now...</i>

579
00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:06.607
<i>I pledged to stand up
for Alabama when I campaigned</i>

580
00:37:06.680 --> 00:37:08.762
<i>and the people elected me
on that pledge,</i>

581
00:37:08.840 --> 00:37:11.241
<i>and that is exactly what I intend to do.</i>

582
00:37:23.120 --> 00:37:24.360
(WOMAN SIGHS)

583
00:37:37.160 --> 00:37:39.288
ABERNATHY: Johnson'll flinch.

584
00:37:39.920 --> 00:37:41.888
KING: I'm tired, Ralphy.

585
00:37:43.880 --> 00:37:45.689
Tiring of this.

586
00:37:46.400 --> 00:37:48.721
Eyes on the prize, Martin.

587
00:37:48.800 --> 00:37:51.644
Yeah, but what is the prize, friend?

588
00:37:52.360 --> 00:37:55.842
We fight to have a seat
at whatever table we want.

589
00:37:56.840 --> 00:37:59.923
How does it help a black man
to be able to eat at a lunch counter

590
00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.480
if he doesn't earn enough
to buy the burger?

591
00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:06.048
Or worse yet, can't even...

592
00:38:08.640 --> 00:38:10.210
Can't even read the menu

593
00:38:10.280 --> 00:38:13.523
'cause there was no Negro school
where he's from.

594
00:38:13.600 --> 00:38:15.648
What is that?

595
00:38:15.720 --> 00:38:16.801
That equality?

596
00:38:19.120 --> 00:38:22.249
- Amen.
- And what about in our minds?

597
00:38:23.040 --> 00:38:26.726
Equality in the black psyche.
Look at these men.

598
00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:31.288
Beaten and broken down for generations.

599
00:38:31.360 --> 00:38:33.727
Deciding to demand more?

600
00:38:35.640 --> 00:38:38.450
What happens when a man stands up
and says enough is enough?

601
00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:40.329
Look at Medgar.

602
00:38:40.400 --> 00:38:43.483
Murdered the man in his own driveway.

603
00:38:43.560 --> 00:38:45.562
Kids and wife right there
inside the house.

604
00:38:45.640 --> 00:38:48.530
George and Herbert Lee, Lamar Smith.

605
00:38:48.600 --> 00:38:51.763
A man stands up, only to be struck down.

606
00:38:54.440 --> 00:38:57.091
And what happens to the people he led?

607
00:39:00.880 --> 00:39:01.961
(SIGHS)

608
00:39:02.040 --> 00:39:03.929
What are we doing, Ralphy?

609
00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:08.401
We take it piece by piece.

610
00:39:08.920 --> 00:39:10.604
Like we been doing.

611
00:39:11.280 --> 00:39:13.567
We build the path as we can.

612
00:39:14.280 --> 00:39:16.169
Rock by rock.

613
00:39:23.280 --> 00:39:25.408
This cell is probably bugged.

614
00:39:26.680 --> 00:39:28.045
(LAUGHING)

615
00:39:28.120 --> 00:39:29.610
It probably is.

616
00:39:33.400 --> 00:39:34.925
Oh, Lord.

617
00:39:40.800 --> 00:39:45.681
They're gonna ruin me
so they can ruin this movement.

618
00:39:47.200 --> 00:39:48.486
They are.

619
00:39:54.680 --> 00:39:56.648
"Look at the birds of the air,

620
00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:01.048
"that they do not sow, nor reap,

621
00:40:01.120 --> 00:40:02.849
"nor gather into barns,

622
00:40:04.160 --> 00:40:06.970
"and yet your Heavenly Father
doth feed them.

623
00:40:09.200 --> 00:40:11.521
"Are you not worth much more than they?

624
00:40:13.160 --> 00:40:16.050
"And who of you by being worried

625
00:40:16.120 --> 00:40:18.646
"can add a single hour to his life?"

626
00:40:19.080 --> 00:40:21.048
Matthew 6, verse 27.

627
00:40:21.120 --> 00:40:22.485
All right.

628
00:40:23.520 --> 00:40:24.760
Yes, sir.

629
00:40:29.120 --> 00:40:30.121
(SIGHS)

630
00:40:31.600 --> 00:40:32.806
VIVIAN: What? Where did you hear that?

631
00:40:32.880 --> 00:40:35.167
ORANGE: I overheard them talking
about him coming in this evening.

632
00:40:35.240 --> 00:40:36.287
LEWIS: Overheard us?

633
00:40:36.360 --> 00:40:38.442
I'm learning about this just like you.
We didn't do this.

634
00:40:38.520 --> 00:40:39.931
WILLIAMS: That Negro
can't be talking about that

635
00:40:40.040 --> 00:40:42.407
"by any means necessary" madness
with these people.

636
00:40:42.480 --> 00:40:43.925
They about to bust as it is.

637
00:40:44.040 --> 00:40:45.087
He's on his way here, right?

638
00:40:45.160 --> 00:40:46.844
So we gotta figure this out.
Right and fast.

639
00:40:46.920 --> 00:40:48.729
Oh, he ain't on his way. He here.

640
00:40:51.240 --> 00:40:52.571
Holy shit.

641
00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:54.369
(CAR DOORS CLOSING)

642
00:41:03.480 --> 00:41:04.720
- Are you all right?
- (EXHALES)

643
00:41:05.800 --> 00:41:09.407
I wish I had more time to prepare is all.

644
00:41:10.360 --> 00:41:13.807
I want to do this kind of thing
whenever possible.

645
00:41:13.880 --> 00:41:16.929
But I don't get to do it enough
to feel entirely comfortable.

646
00:41:19.280 --> 00:41:20.691
I prefer to be prepared.

647
00:41:21.240 --> 00:41:23.322
Yes, I understand that.

648
00:41:24.120 --> 00:41:26.885
I admire you. I do.

649
00:41:28.240 --> 00:41:31.403
Sometimes I wish
I were more out there in the trenches.

650
00:41:31.480 --> 00:41:33.721
You do more than you know, Mrs. King.

651
00:41:33.800 --> 00:41:34.801
(CORETTA EXHALES)

652
00:41:36.480 --> 00:41:39.165
I'll tell you what I know to be true.

653
00:41:39.240 --> 00:41:42.005
It helps me in times
when I'm feeling unsure.

654
00:41:42.080 --> 00:41:43.081
If you'd like.

655
00:41:43.920 --> 00:41:45.763
Oh, please do, Mrs. Boynton.

656
00:41:48.120 --> 00:41:51.681
I know that we are descendants
of a mighty people,

657
00:41:51.760 --> 00:41:54.286
who gave civilization to the world.

658
00:41:55.280 --> 00:41:58.329
People who survived
the hulls of slave ships

659
00:41:58.400 --> 00:42:00.289
across vast oceans.

660
00:42:00.360 --> 00:42:04.684
People who innovate and create and love

661
00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:09.049
despite pressures
and tortures unimaginable.

662
00:42:10.040 --> 00:42:11.963
They are in our bloodstream.

663
00:42:12.040 --> 00:42:14.646
Pumping our hearts every second.

664
00:42:16.120 --> 00:42:17.929
They've prepared you.

665
00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:21.964
You are already prepared.

666
00:42:22.120 --> 00:42:24.885
Mrs. King, I mean no disrespect.

667
00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:29.123
I come with great respect
for your husband.

668
00:42:30.040 --> 00:42:32.407
I have no army behind me anymore.

669
00:42:33.440 --> 00:42:36.250
I have myself and the truth.

670
00:42:37.120 --> 00:42:39.487
That is all I stand on today.

671
00:42:39.560 --> 00:42:42.848
You've said disrespectful things
in the past, Minister.

672
00:42:42.920 --> 00:42:45.571
So you'll understand
why there is some alarm here tonight.

673
00:42:45.640 --> 00:42:47.961
I do. I understand that.

674
00:42:48.920 --> 00:42:52.049
Your husband and I, we do not see
exactly eye-to-eye

675
00:42:52.120 --> 00:42:54.327
on how to achieve progress
for the black man.

676
00:42:54.400 --> 00:42:58.166
And yes, I have been piercing
in my critiques of non-violence.

677
00:42:58.240 --> 00:43:02.450
But because we don't agree, Mrs. King,
does not mean that I'm the enemy.

678
00:43:02.520 --> 00:43:05.763
What do you intend to say
to these people then, sir?

679
00:43:05.840 --> 00:43:07.251
A lot of work has been done here,

680
00:43:07.320 --> 00:43:09.322
and I don't intend to
see it undone tonight.

681
00:43:11.480 --> 00:43:14.882
Let's just say, my eyes see in a new way.

682
00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:18.526
But your local sheriff here?
He doesn't know that.

683
00:43:19.440 --> 00:43:21.761
So allow me to be the alternative
to your husband.

684
00:43:22.880 --> 00:43:24.769
The alternative
that scares them so much

685
00:43:24.840 --> 00:43:26.649
they turn to Dr. King in refuge.

686
00:43:26.720 --> 00:43:29.121
Let my being here, Mrs. King,
represent the factions

687
00:43:29.200 --> 00:43:31.851
that will come if they don't
give the good reverend

688
00:43:31.960 --> 00:43:34.201
what he's asking for and soon.

689
00:43:34.280 --> 00:43:37.090
Do you know what he has said
about us in the past, Coretta?

690
00:43:37.160 --> 00:43:40.004
He called us "ignorant Negro preachers."

691
00:43:40.080 --> 00:43:41.969
Called me a modern day Uncle Tom.

692
00:43:42.040 --> 00:43:45.089
Said on national television
that the white man pays me

693
00:43:45.160 --> 00:43:48.289
to keep Negroes defenseless.

694
00:43:48.360 --> 00:43:51.204
The white man pays me!

695
00:43:53.240 --> 00:43:55.402
How could you allow it?

696
00:43:55.480 --> 00:43:59.087
It wasn't like that this time, Martin.
I'm telling you...

697
00:43:59.160 --> 00:44:01.606
He spoke with some of
the words he's used before,

698
00:44:01.680 --> 00:44:03.569
but it wasn't aimed at you.

699
00:44:04.120 --> 00:44:05.531
It was...

700
00:44:06.160 --> 00:44:07.571
It had more to do with helping us.

701
00:44:09.920 --> 00:44:11.251
Not that you need his help.

702
00:44:11.320 --> 00:44:12.651
I'm just telling you how it was.

703
00:44:12.720 --> 00:44:15.451
This movement, our movement,

704
00:44:15.520 --> 00:44:17.727
has been the one
that has moved the needle.

705
00:44:17.840 --> 00:44:19.842
Our movement changes laws

706
00:44:19.920 --> 00:44:21.490
and day-to-day life for our people.

707
00:44:21.560 --> 00:44:23.608
But what has he changed?

708
00:44:23.720 --> 00:44:26.087
Actually changed?

709
00:44:28.600 --> 00:44:31.285
You don't sound like yourself.
You sound tired.

710
00:44:31.360 --> 00:44:33.249
And you sound enamored.

711
00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:40.889
(CORETTA SIGHS)

712
00:44:40.960 --> 00:44:42.325
I didn't mean that.

713
00:44:43.280 --> 00:44:44.645
Corrie.

714
00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:48.604
Coretta.

715
00:44:49.760 --> 00:44:51.330
I didn't mean that.

716
00:45:02.200 --> 00:45:03.406
(CORETTA SIGHS)

717
00:45:06.040 --> 00:45:07.371
I'm tired.

718
00:45:09.080 --> 00:45:10.730
You're right.

719
00:45:18.200 --> 00:45:19.645
Rest then.

720
00:45:21.320 --> 00:45:22.481
Rest tonight, Martin.

721
00:45:24.920 --> 00:45:28.049
WALLACE: <i>This is not
what I want to hear.</i>

722
00:45:28.760 --> 00:45:32.082
How in Christ's sake does
Malcolm X slip into my state,

723
00:45:32.160 --> 00:45:34.891
meet with the wife of the other one,

724
00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:36.923
and give an actual speech
to these nigras

725
00:45:37.000 --> 00:45:38.411
who are already riled up enough?

726
00:45:38.480 --> 00:45:40.244
I mean, how does that happen,
Colonel Lingo?

727
00:45:40.320 --> 00:45:41.401
Governor...

728
00:45:41.480 --> 00:45:44.609
Is every spook militant in existence
gonna pay us a visit?

729
00:45:46.080 --> 00:45:48.082
- Huh?
- (SIGHS)

730
00:45:48.160 --> 00:45:49.924
Do you know what this means?

731
00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:51.968
Johnson is going to get jumpy.

732
00:45:53.080 --> 00:45:56.766
King and X together is sending him
through the cotton-pickin' stratosphere.

733
00:45:56.840 --> 00:45:59.571
And pictures of nigras
getting beat in the street

734
00:45:59.640 --> 00:46:00.846
- doesn't help the matter.
- Governor...

735
00:46:00.920 --> 00:46:04.049
Now I can't make a move
against that backwoods,

736
00:46:04.120 --> 00:46:05.565
white trash Sheriff Clark

737
00:46:05.640 --> 00:46:07.244
'cause that'll be seen
as I'm helping King.

738
00:46:07.320 --> 00:46:11.370
But somebody got to
get Jim Clark under control.

739
00:46:12.240 --> 00:46:13.651
Election year is coming up

740
00:46:13.720 --> 00:46:16.963
and this black voting business
won't abide.

741
00:46:17.040 --> 00:46:18.724
I mean, what's not clear about that?

742
00:46:18.800 --> 00:46:21.007
Look, George, I'm telling you,

743
00:46:21.080 --> 00:46:23.731
if the Lord Jesus and Elvis Presley

744
00:46:23.840 --> 00:46:25.808
come visiting and they said,

745
00:46:25.880 --> 00:46:29.965
"Jim, now, we need you to
treat them niggers nice."

746
00:46:30.040 --> 00:46:32.691
Jim Clark would beat the shit
out of the pair of them,

747
00:46:32.760 --> 00:46:33.841
then throw them in jail.

748
00:46:35.200 --> 00:46:36.531
Jesus H. Christ.

749
00:46:36.600 --> 00:46:39.444
Jim's a good old boy,
he's a friend of mine.

750
00:46:39.520 --> 00:46:41.045
Jim Clark just ain't that scary.

751
00:46:42.640 --> 00:46:44.722
Now he's playing into their hands.

752
00:46:45.760 --> 00:46:47.285
Now...

753
00:46:47.360 --> 00:46:49.840
If you want fear,

754
00:46:50.800 --> 00:46:53.451
you need dominance in Selma.

755
00:46:54.680 --> 00:47:00.084
Hoover picked up some intel
about a night march.

756
00:47:00.160 --> 00:47:01.321
Wasn't announced.

757
00:47:01.400 --> 00:47:03.289
It's some locals outside of King's group.

758
00:47:03.360 --> 00:47:05.567
Unofficial, they called it.

759
00:47:05.640 --> 00:47:10.089
Supposed to happen tomorrow night
once King leaves jail.

760
00:47:10.160 --> 00:47:12.766
Going to some bleeding heart
fundraiser in California.

761
00:47:18.120 --> 00:47:19.645
WALLACE: <i>So...</i>

762
00:47:20.560 --> 00:47:22.483
King's out of town.

763
00:47:23.520 --> 00:47:24.646
Fewer cameras.

764
00:47:26.440 --> 00:47:27.521
And at night.

765
00:47:27.600 --> 00:47:30.331
LINGO: <i>Find a reason
to send us in there.</i>

766
00:47:30.400 --> 00:47:33.927
<i>Let's scare some real sense
into them black bastards.</i>

767
00:47:34.000 --> 00:47:35.525
OFFICER: (OVER LOUDSPEAKER)
<i>Y'all move back.</i>

768
00:47:35.600 --> 00:47:37.284
<i>Move back now. Get back.</i>

769
00:47:38.120 --> 00:47:39.531
<i>Go back to your homes now.</i>

770
00:47:39.600 --> 00:47:40.681
(OFFICER BLOWING WHISTLE)

771
00:47:40.760 --> 00:47:41.761
(ALL SCREAMING)

772
00:47:55.120 --> 00:47:57.361
- Stop! Leave him be!
- Mama, come on!

773
00:47:58.120 --> 00:47:59.724
Mama, come on!

774
00:48:00.760 --> 00:48:02.569
We gotta keep moving. Come on.

775
00:48:05.840 --> 00:48:07.046
This way, this way.

776
00:48:07.120 --> 00:48:08.201
WOMAN: Leave him alone.

777
00:48:09.480 --> 00:48:10.641
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

778
00:48:15.960 --> 00:48:17.450
(JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)

779
00:48:19.200 --> 00:48:20.565
(ALL PANTING)

780
00:48:24.880 --> 00:48:26.086
It's all right.

781
00:48:30.160 --> 00:48:32.049
It's gonna be all right. Okay?

782
00:48:32.120 --> 00:48:34.361
Act like you're...
Act like you're reading your menu. Okay?

783
00:48:35.680 --> 00:48:36.761
It's okay.

784
00:48:37.920 --> 00:48:39.001
Pops...

785
00:48:40.120 --> 00:48:43.203
It's all right, Mama. It's gonna be cool.

786
00:48:43.280 --> 00:48:44.850
It's okay, it's okay.

787
00:48:50.600 --> 00:48:51.601
JIMMIE: Hey! Hey...

788
00:48:51.680 --> 00:48:53.125
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

789
00:48:56.400 --> 00:48:59.131
No, get off of him! Just get off of him!

790
00:48:59.200 --> 00:49:01.601
Get off of him! No!

791
00:49:02.400 --> 00:49:04.084
No! Get off of him!

792
00:49:04.160 --> 00:49:05.286
- (GROANS)
- (VIOLA SCREAMING)

793
00:49:07.880 --> 00:49:09.245
VIOLA: Stop it! No, no, no!

794
00:49:11.240 --> 00:49:12.366
- (COCKING GUN)
- Stop it!

795
00:49:34.920 --> 00:49:36.285
(VIOLA WAILING)

796
00:49:39.200 --> 00:49:40.247
Help me.

797
00:49:40.480 --> 00:49:42.608
(SIRENS BLARING IN DISTANCE)

798
00:49:43.040 --> 00:49:44.246
(CRYING)

799
00:49:53.080 --> 00:49:54.320
Help me.

800
00:49:55.480 --> 00:49:56.720
Jimmie.

801
00:49:58.160 --> 00:50:00.925
Jimmie. Jimmie. Jimmie.

802
00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:02.047
Help me.

803
00:50:21.400 --> 00:50:22.765
Sir?

804
00:50:28.400 --> 00:50:30.641
Oh. Dr. King.

805
00:50:47.960 --> 00:50:52.010
There are no words
to soothe you, Mr. Lee.

806
00:50:54.480 --> 00:50:56.323
There are no words.

807
00:50:59.640 --> 00:51:02.450
But I can tell you one thing for certain.

808
00:51:05.800 --> 00:51:07.290
God was the first to cry.

809
00:51:07.360 --> 00:51:08.771
Yes.

810
00:51:10.200 --> 00:51:12.009
He was the first to cry for your boy.

811
00:51:12.080 --> 00:51:13.844
Yes. I believe that.

812
00:51:17.720 --> 00:51:19.449
Is your daughter...

813
00:51:20.720 --> 00:51:23.644
Is Jimmie Lee's mother here, Mr. Lee?

814
00:51:25.200 --> 00:51:28.682
No, she... She couldn't make it.

815
00:51:35.640 --> 00:51:37.449
May I ask your age, sir?

816
00:51:39.200 --> 00:51:41.567
Well, I... I got 82 years.

817
00:51:42.360 --> 00:51:43.805
1883.

818
00:51:43.880 --> 00:51:45.086
Right.

819
00:51:45.160 --> 00:51:47.242
(STAMMERING) Yeah. Jimmie...

820
00:51:50.840 --> 00:51:52.888
He born in '38.

821
00:51:54.360 --> 00:51:56.044
He a Army man.

822
00:51:56.120 --> 00:51:58.691
I mean, he was... Was an Army man.

823
00:51:58.800 --> 00:52:01.087
In the Army a spell.

824
00:52:02.720 --> 00:52:07.408
He say, "Pa, you gonna vote
before you done."

825
00:52:07.520 --> 00:52:09.363
Mmm-hmm. That's what he said.

826
00:52:11.560 --> 00:52:12.891
He tell me.

827
00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:17.563
- He was a good boy.
- Yes.

828
00:52:17.640 --> 00:52:18.721
Always good.

829
00:52:19.720 --> 00:52:21.484
Always good.

830
00:52:28.840 --> 00:52:30.524
Jimmie gone.

831
00:52:35.920 --> 00:52:37.729
I'm so sorry.

832
00:52:43.720 --> 00:52:44.801
Yeah.

833
00:53:00.680 --> 00:53:06.005
KING: <i>Who murdered
Jimmie Lee Jackson?</i>

834
00:53:10.280 --> 00:53:14.080
<i>Who murdered Jimmie Lee Jackson?</i>

835
00:53:16.480 --> 00:53:18.960
<i>We know a state trooper</i>

836
00:53:19.040 --> 00:53:21.247
<i>acting under the orders
of George Wallace</i>

837
00:53:21.320 --> 00:53:23.721
<i>pointed the gun and pulled the trigger.</i>

838
00:53:25.240 --> 00:53:29.131
<i>But how many other fingers
were on that trigger?</i>

839
00:53:32.320 --> 00:53:34.561
<i>Who murdered Jimmie Lee Jackson?</i>

840
00:53:36.960 --> 00:53:41.648
<i>Every white lawman
who abuses the law to terrorize.</i>

841
00:53:44.720 --> 00:53:46.802
<i>Every white politician</i>

842
00:53:47.680 --> 00:53:50.729
<i>who feeds on prejudice and hatred.</i>

843
00:53:50.800 --> 00:53:52.928
(ALL AGREEING)

844
00:53:53.040 --> 00:53:56.726
<i>Every white preacher
who preaches the Bible</i>

845
00:53:56.800 --> 00:53:59.565
<i>and stays silent
before his white congregation.</i>

846
00:53:59.640 --> 00:54:01.324
(ALL AGREEING)

847
00:54:03.840 --> 00:54:06.684
<i>Who murdered Jimmie Lee Jackson?</i>

848
00:54:07.840 --> 00:54:10.525
<i>Every Negro man and woman</i>

849
00:54:10.640 --> 00:54:13.723
<i>who stands by without joining this fight</i>

850
00:54:13.800 --> 00:54:16.724
<i>as their brothers and sisters
are humiliated,</i>

851
00:54:16.800 --> 00:54:19.690
<i>brutalized, and ripped from this earth!</i>

852
00:54:19.760 --> 00:54:21.842
(APPLAUSE)

853
00:54:27.000 --> 00:54:28.889
<i>When I heard</i>

854
00:54:28.960 --> 00:54:32.328
<i>President Kennedy
had been shot and killed...</i>

855
00:54:33.800 --> 00:54:36.371
<i>And when I heard just yesterday</i>

856
00:54:36.440 --> 00:54:38.249
<i>that Malcolm X,</i>

857
00:54:38.320 --> 00:54:41.563
<i>who stood in this very church
just three weeks ago,</i>

858
00:54:41.640 --> 00:54:43.642
<i>had been shot and killed,</i>

859
00:54:45.440 --> 00:54:47.761
<i>I turned to my wife Coretta</i>

860
00:54:47.840 --> 00:54:49.808
<i>and said the same thing I often say</i>

861
00:54:49.880 --> 00:54:52.531
<i>when one of our leaders is struck down,</i>

862
00:54:54.400 --> 00:54:57.483
<i>"Our lives are not fully lived</i>

863
00:54:57.560 --> 00:55:00.609
<i>"if we're not willing to die
for those we love</i>

864
00:55:01.160 --> 00:55:02.650
<i>"and for what we believe."</i>

865
00:55:02.720 --> 00:55:04.051
(ALL AGREEING)

866
00:55:06.880 --> 00:55:08.405
<i>But today, Jimmie,</i>

867
00:55:09.360 --> 00:55:13.126
<i>we're doing the living
and you've done the dying, dear brother.</i>

868
00:55:14.120 --> 00:55:18.330
<i>We will not let your sacrifice
pass in vain, dear brother.</i>

869
00:55:18.400 --> 00:55:20.323
<i>We will not let it go!</i>

870
00:55:20.400 --> 00:55:22.641
<i>We will finish what you were after!</i>

871
00:55:22.720 --> 00:55:25.121
<i>We will get what you were denied!</i>

872
00:55:25.200 --> 00:55:28.727
<i>We will vote and we will
put these men out of office!</i>

873
00:55:28.800 --> 00:55:30.802
<i>We will take their power!</i>

874
00:55:30.880 --> 00:55:33.326
<i>We will win
what you were slaughtered for!</i>

875
00:55:33.400 --> 00:55:34.811
PEOPLE: Yeah!

876
00:55:38.120 --> 00:55:40.361
<i>We're going back to Washington.</i>

877
00:55:41.080 --> 00:55:43.082
<i>We're going to demand
to see the President.</i>

878
00:55:43.160 --> 00:55:44.730
<i>And I'm gonna tell him</i>

879
00:55:45.440 --> 00:55:48.683
<i>that Jimmie was murdered
by an administration</i>

880
00:55:48.760 --> 00:55:51.650
<i>that spends millions of dollars every day</i>

881
00:55:51.720 --> 00:55:55.441
<i>to sacrifice life
in the name of liberty in Vietnam,</i>

882
00:55:55.520 --> 00:55:58.126
<i>yet lacks the moral will
and the moral courage</i>

883
00:55:58.200 --> 00:56:02.171
<i>to defend the lives
of its own people here in America!</i>

884
00:56:02.240 --> 00:56:03.765
(APPLAUSE)

885
00:56:04.560 --> 00:56:06.449
<i>We will not let it go!</i>

886
00:56:07.560 --> 00:56:11.406
<i>And if he does not act,
we will act. We will act!</i>

887
00:56:11.480 --> 00:56:13.369
<i>We will do it for all of our lost ones.</i>

888
00:56:13.920 --> 00:56:16.241
<i>All of those, like Jimmie Lee Jackson,</i>

889
00:56:16.320 --> 00:56:17.890
<i>who have gone too soon,</i>

890
00:56:17.960 --> 00:56:20.042
<i>taken by hate!</i>

891
00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:21.724
(APPLAUSE)

892
00:56:28.160 --> 00:56:29.844
Let me hear the top-tier issues

893
00:56:29.920 --> 00:56:33.891
that have to be evident
in the overall legislation we demand.

894
00:56:33.960 --> 00:56:35.041
Let's break it down.

895
00:56:35.160 --> 00:56:37.640
But let's root this discussion
in what we know.

896
00:56:38.400 --> 00:56:40.926
We know Johnson
can't see the full picture.

897
00:56:41.040 --> 00:56:42.769
So, let's paint it for him.

898
00:56:42.840 --> 00:56:46.970
What are the specific hardships
and humiliations

899
00:56:47.040 --> 00:56:51.011
we can address
within the larger context of legislation?

900
00:56:52.440 --> 00:56:55.922
Doc, we gotta start
with banning these laws that

901
00:56:56.000 --> 00:56:58.162
if a Negro tries to register,

902
00:56:58.240 --> 00:57:00.971
I mean, actually musters up
the courage to go in that courthouse,

903
00:57:01.680 --> 00:57:04.763
that their name and address
is published in the paper.

904
00:57:04.840 --> 00:57:07.207
It gives anybody who wants
to do them any harm

905
00:57:07.280 --> 00:57:09.965
their exact location,
and we know how the Klan is.

906
00:57:10.040 --> 00:57:12.805
I hear that. But the poll taxes
got to be our focus first.

907
00:57:12.880 --> 00:57:13.961
'Cause black people are poor!

908
00:57:14.040 --> 00:57:15.849
- Black people are poor down here.
- Yep.

909
00:57:15.920 --> 00:57:18.287
And they expected to pay for every year
they weren't legally registered

910
00:57:18.360 --> 00:57:19.441
before they can register.

911
00:57:19.520 --> 00:57:22.126
Now, what the hell is that?
Who got that kind of money?

912
00:57:22.200 --> 00:57:24.282
(ALL CLAMORING)

913
00:57:24.360 --> 00:57:25.771
VIVIAN: Come on now! Listen now!

914
00:57:25.840 --> 00:57:28.161
The big issue is voting vouchers.

915
00:57:28.240 --> 00:57:29.446
Is that the number one issue?

916
00:57:29.520 --> 00:57:30.601
VIVIAN: Now hold on. Let me finish.

917
00:57:30.680 --> 00:57:32.205
'Cause everybody'll forget
about this part.

918
00:57:32.280 --> 00:57:35.124
But if you're Negro,
the only way you can vote

919
00:57:35.200 --> 00:57:37.806
is if an approved registered voter
vouches for you.

920
00:57:37.880 --> 00:57:40.929
Right? So, let's say, you take
some place like Lowndes County,

921
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:43.207
where there are no Negroes
who are registered

922
00:57:43.280 --> 00:57:47.126
and you've got to have someone
who is registered to vouch for you.

923
00:57:47.200 --> 00:57:48.406
What are you supposed to do?

924
00:57:48.600 --> 00:57:49.761
- Hmm?
- Mmm.

925
00:57:49.840 --> 00:57:51.444
Nobody you know,

926
00:57:51.520 --> 00:57:55.764
not a single black person
for 100 miles is registered.

927
00:57:55.840 --> 00:57:59.367
So how do you get the voucher, right?

928
00:57:59.440 --> 00:58:01.807
To get you into the courthouse door

929
00:58:01.880 --> 00:58:04.281
to pay the poll tax

930
00:58:04.360 --> 00:58:06.681
to get your name published

931
00:58:07.080 --> 00:58:08.320
and get yourself dead.

932
00:58:09.920 --> 00:58:11.001
That's true.

933
00:58:11.080 --> 00:58:12.491
We need a new plan!

934
00:58:12.560 --> 00:58:14.164
I can't take him back to Washington

935
00:58:14.240 --> 00:58:17.050
and waltz into the White House
with a list of empty demands.

936
00:58:17.120 --> 00:58:19.009
Tactics, my friends!

937
00:58:19.080 --> 00:58:21.731
We must break down this institution

938
00:58:21.800 --> 00:58:24.644
into the tangible tactics
that it takes to dismantle it.

939
00:58:27.080 --> 00:58:28.161
JOHNSON: <i>What's your next move?</i>

940
00:58:28.240 --> 00:58:32.484
A march from Selma to Montgomery
to protest and amplify.

941
00:58:32.560 --> 00:58:34.528
Well, I'll be damned.

942
00:58:34.600 --> 00:58:37.001
This was always
part of the plan, wasn't it?

943
00:58:37.080 --> 00:58:40.004
Provoke some tragedy
in little old Selma, then go big.

944
00:58:40.600 --> 00:58:43.968
Get someone killed
and march on the State Capitol!

945
00:58:44.400 --> 00:58:47.085
Selma to Montgomery's
gotta be 50 miles!

946
00:58:47.160 --> 00:58:49.891
You march those people
into rural Alabama unprotected,

947
00:58:49.960 --> 00:58:51.121
it's gonna be open season.

948
00:58:51.200 --> 00:58:53.646
It's too damn far
and too damn dangerous!

949
00:58:53.720 --> 00:58:55.609
Then propose new legislation, sir.

950
00:58:55.680 --> 00:58:58.331
I can't do that this year.
I won't! I told you.

951
00:58:58.840 --> 00:59:00.842
We need your involvement here,
Mr. President.

952
00:59:00.920 --> 00:59:03.571
We deserve your help
as citizens of this country.

953
00:59:03.640 --> 00:59:04.721
Citizens under attack.

954
00:59:04.800 --> 00:59:07.929
Now, you listen to me. You listen to me.

955
00:59:08.000 --> 00:59:09.889
You're an activist. I'm a politician.

956
00:59:09.960 --> 00:59:12.566
You got one big issue.
I got a hundred and one.

957
00:59:12.640 --> 00:59:14.608
Now, you demanding more

958
00:59:14.680 --> 00:59:17.047
and putting me on the spot
with this visit, that's okay.

959
00:59:17.120 --> 00:59:18.884
That's your job. That's what you do.

960
00:59:18.960 --> 00:59:21.531
But I am sick and tired

961
00:59:21.600 --> 00:59:23.887
of you demanding and telling me

962
00:59:23.960 --> 00:59:26.281
what I can and what I can't do.

963
00:59:26.360 --> 00:59:28.089
If you want my support
on this voting thing,

964
00:59:28.160 --> 00:59:30.162
I need some quid pro quo from you.

965
00:59:30.640 --> 00:59:32.051
What do you want, Mr. President?

966
00:59:32.640 --> 00:59:36.008
We have a line on
some threats that are, uh,

967
00:59:36.960 --> 00:59:38.405
particularly troubling.

968
00:59:38.520 --> 00:59:40.249
Well, what's new?

969
00:59:40.320 --> 00:59:44.928
No, no. This is serious.
Credible threats with detail.

970
00:59:45.000 --> 00:59:47.685
RUSTIN: This information,
coming from the FBI, I assume?

971
00:59:48.760 --> 00:59:49.886
High-level?

972
00:59:50.520 --> 00:59:53.888
The same high-level
that's been tracking us like animals?

973
00:59:53.960 --> 00:59:57.123
Bugging our homes and our hotel rooms.

974
00:59:58.120 --> 01:00:01.727
Digging for things
that simply are not there, Lee?

975
01:00:02.840 --> 01:00:05.320
This all feels very convenient.

976
01:00:06.520 --> 01:00:07.760
WHITE: Okay.

977
01:00:08.280 --> 01:00:10.760
This is coming from
Lowndes County, Alabama.

978
01:00:10.840 --> 01:00:12.922
Between Selma and Montgomery.

979
01:00:14.720 --> 01:00:17.963
I'm telling you, if he were my guy,

980
01:00:18.040 --> 01:00:20.407
I'd keep him off the frontlines.

981
01:00:21.240 --> 01:00:22.446
Just for a while.

982
01:00:25.520 --> 01:00:26.885
Not gonna happen, Lee.

983
01:00:27.400 --> 01:00:29.164
Meet me halfway on this, Martin.

984
01:00:29.240 --> 01:00:31.288
I can't, Mr. President.

985
01:00:31.360 --> 01:00:33.124
Can't or won't?

986
01:00:33.200 --> 01:00:37.410
I came here hoping
to talk to you about people.

987
01:00:38.320 --> 01:00:40.891
People are dying in the street for this.

988
01:00:40.960 --> 01:00:43.440
It cannot wait, sir.

989
01:00:44.440 --> 01:00:46.044
Mr. President, how did it go?

990
01:00:51.840 --> 01:00:53.490
What can I do to help?

991
01:00:56.400 --> 01:00:58.289
Get me J. Edgar Hoover.

992
01:00:59.760 --> 01:01:01.091
MAN 1: (ON TAPE) <i>King,</i>

993
01:01:01.920 --> 01:01:04.002
<i>you know you are a complete fraud</i>

994
01:01:04.080 --> 01:01:07.129
<i>and a liability to all nigras.</i>

995
01:01:07.200 --> 01:01:10.329
<i>Like all frauds, your end is approaching.</i>

996
01:01:11.240 --> 01:01:12.810
<i>You are done.</i>

997
01:01:13.600 --> 01:01:17.889
<i>Your degrees and your fancy awards
will not save you.</i>

998
01:01:18.880 --> 01:01:23.807
<i>The American public
will soon know you for what you are,</i>

999
01:01:23.880 --> 01:01:27.202
<i>an evil, abnormal beast.</i>

1000
01:01:27.280 --> 01:01:29.851
(MAN 2 GRUNTING ON TAPE)

1001
01:01:29.920 --> 01:01:32.161
(WOMAN MOANING ON TAPE)

1002
01:01:36.320 --> 01:01:37.731
(TAPE STOPS)

1003
01:01:45.400 --> 01:01:46.970
That wasn't me.

1004
01:01:49.960 --> 01:01:51.689
That isn't me, Corrie.

1005
01:01:56.160 --> 01:01:57.491
I know.

1006
01:01:59.960 --> 01:02:02.611
I know what you sound like.

1007
01:02:12.680 --> 01:02:14.728
I've gotten used to a lot.

1008
01:02:17.680 --> 01:02:21.526
All the hours wondering after your safety,

1009
01:02:23.000 --> 01:02:25.321
worried about how you are.

1010
01:02:30.360 --> 01:02:31.441
This house.

1011
01:02:33.680 --> 01:02:34.886
Renting here.

1012
01:02:37.120 --> 01:02:38.724
No foundation.

1013
01:02:44.040 --> 01:02:46.771
Without the things
the children should have,

1014
01:02:46.840 --> 01:02:49.002
all because of how it would look.

1015
01:02:54.480 --> 01:02:56.244
I have gotten used to it,

1016
01:02:57.680 --> 01:02:59.330
for better or worse.

1017
01:03:02.480 --> 01:03:03.891
(SIGHS)

1018
01:03:04.680 --> 01:03:07.365
But what I have never gotten used to

1019
01:03:08.360 --> 01:03:09.850
is the death.

1020
01:03:12.200 --> 01:03:16.683
The constant closeness of death.

1021
01:03:19.720 --> 01:03:21.449
(CORETTA SIGHS)

1022
01:03:21.520 --> 01:03:24.251
It's become like a thick fog to me.

1023
01:03:26.720 --> 01:03:29.451
I can't see life sometimes

1024
01:03:29.520 --> 01:03:33.730
because of the fog of death
constantly hanging over.

1025
01:03:37.400 --> 01:03:41.007
People actually say
that they will stop the blood

1026
01:03:41.080 --> 01:03:44.482
running through the hearts
of our children.

1027
01:03:44.560 --> 01:03:47.530
That's what they said
on the other end of that phone line.

1028
01:03:51.200 --> 01:03:53.806
How they're going to kill my children.

1029
01:03:54.600 --> 01:03:57.001
And what they'll do to you
and how they'll do it.

1030
01:03:57.080 --> 01:03:59.481
How many years
have I had to listen to this?

1031
01:03:59.560 --> 01:04:00.686
The filth,

1032
01:04:00.760 --> 01:04:06.449
deranged and twisted
and just ignorant enough to be serious.

1033
01:04:13.560 --> 01:04:15.369
If I ask you something,

1034
01:04:17.080 --> 01:04:20.448
will you answer me with the truth?

1035
01:04:22.440 --> 01:04:23.521
Yes.

1036
01:04:25.240 --> 01:04:26.685
Good,

1037
01:04:26.800 --> 01:04:29.451
because I am not a fool.

1038
01:04:38.440 --> 01:04:40.283
Do you love me?

1039
01:04:47.200 --> 01:04:49.567
Yes, I love you, Coretta.

1040
01:04:59.880 --> 01:05:01.086
(SNIFFLES)

1041
01:05:01.160 --> 01:05:03.367
Do you love any of the others?

1042
01:05:25.240 --> 01:05:26.287
No.

1043
01:05:44.440 --> 01:05:46.966
I need to put the march back a day.

1044
01:05:47.440 --> 01:05:48.441
YOUNG: <i>Why?</i>

1045
01:05:49.880 --> 01:05:52.042
<i>I have to be home right now.</i>

1046
01:05:52.680 --> 01:05:53.727
YOUNG: <i>Oh.</i>

1047
01:05:55.720 --> 01:05:58.451
<i>Yes. Okay. I understand.</i>

1048
01:06:01.720 --> 01:06:05.611
<i>But I have to tell you
the organization looks good.</i>

1049
01:06:05.680 --> 01:06:07.205
<i>Real good.</i>

1050
01:06:07.280 --> 01:06:10.409
<i>The mood is strong.
And the locals are prepared.</i>

1051
01:06:10.720 --> 01:06:12.404
<i>The SNCC kids are ready to go.</i>

1052
01:06:12.520 --> 01:06:15.330
<i>We can start it off from Selma,</i>

1053
01:06:15.400 --> 01:06:18.529
<i>and you can join in on the second day.</i>

1054
01:06:30.920 --> 01:06:33.321
<i>I just think it'd be a mistake
to hold people back</i>

1055
01:06:33.400 --> 01:06:34.925
<i>when their blood is up.</i>

1056
01:06:36.360 --> 01:06:38.249
KING: <i>I hear you,</i>

1057
01:06:38.320 --> 01:06:40.004
<i>but we need to be out there full throttle.</i>

1058
01:06:40.080 --> 01:06:41.491
<i>This ain't a test run.</i>

1059
01:06:42.720 --> 01:06:44.165
<i>We need to get to Montgomery.</i>

1060
01:06:44.240 --> 01:06:47.005
<i>I warned Johnson that
we were going to the Capitol.</i>

1061
01:06:47.080 --> 01:06:48.889
<i>We need to do just that.</i>

1062
01:06:49.760 --> 01:06:53.082
YOUNG: <i>And I believe we will.
We'll get there.</i>

1063
01:06:56.920 --> 01:06:59.207
<i>And when we do the real deal, the finale,</i>

1064
01:06:59.280 --> 01:07:01.362
<i>when you make the big speech
at the end,</i>

1065
01:07:01.440 --> 01:07:03.681
<i>right on Wallace's doorstep.</i>

1066
01:07:18.440 --> 01:07:20.886
KING: <i>I don't know, Andy.</i>

1067
01:07:22.200 --> 01:07:24.043
YOUNG: <i>It'll be just fine.</i>

1068
01:07:24.640 --> 01:07:28.281
<i>We'll get it started strong.
And you'll finish strong.</i>

1069
01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:30.081
Mmm.

1070
01:07:34.760 --> 01:07:36.967
Okay. Uh... Let's proceed.

1071
01:07:37.640 --> 01:07:39.563
<i>But only one of us walks to start.</i>

1072
01:07:39.640 --> 01:07:43.611
<i>I don't want to get back on Monday
and find all our leadership in jail.</i>

1073
01:07:44.480 --> 01:07:45.720
<i>One of us walks.</i>

1074
01:07:46.320 --> 01:07:47.810
YOUNG: <i>Understood.</i>

1075
01:07:50.640 --> 01:07:54.770
<i>There will be no march
from Selma to Montgomery.</i>

1076
01:07:55.160 --> 01:07:58.767
<i>It is not conducive to
traffic flow on Route 80.</i>

1077
01:07:58.840 --> 01:08:00.251
<i>Or to public safety.</i>

1078
01:08:00.320 --> 01:08:01.924
Your lives could be in danger,

1079
01:08:02.000 --> 01:08:04.241
but we're going to be strong
if we stick together.

1080
01:08:04.320 --> 01:08:07.529
Don't fight back.
It's a non-violent movement.

1081
01:08:08.000 --> 01:08:11.004
Non-violence is not passive.
It's actually very strong.

1082
01:08:11.640 --> 01:08:13.051
We shouldn't do this, John.

1083
01:08:13.120 --> 01:08:14.929
This is not us. This is not SNCC.

1084
01:08:15.000 --> 01:08:16.206
It's some bullshit.

1085
01:08:16.320 --> 01:08:19.529
It's gonna do more for King
and the SCLC than for Selma.

1086
01:08:19.920 --> 01:08:21.081
This is Alabama.

1087
01:08:21.200 --> 01:08:23.567
They can keep their asses
in Washington, D.C.

1088
01:08:23.640 --> 01:08:25.881
You don't tell us how to live our lives.

1089
01:08:25.960 --> 01:08:28.281
This is an example of what
you might deal with out there.

1090
01:08:28.360 --> 01:08:31.045
What you might experience.
Here we go. Let's show them.

1091
01:08:31.120 --> 01:08:33.441
We don't want your kind here.

1092
01:08:33.520 --> 01:08:35.124
Go to the bottom of the river, black boy.

1093
01:08:35.200 --> 01:08:36.804
<i>We're going to put you down
in Alabama River!</i>

1094
01:08:36.880 --> 01:08:37.927
LEWIS: <i>He's not even here.</i>

1095
01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:39.047
<i>How's it gonna do more for him?</i>

1096
01:08:39.120 --> 01:08:40.963
FORMAN: <i>Well, why ain't
he here, then, man?</i>

1097
01:08:41.040 --> 01:08:42.963
Are you listening to yourself?

1098
01:08:43.040 --> 01:08:45.361
First, it's gonna do more for him.
Now, it's why he ain't here?

1099
01:08:45.440 --> 01:08:46.885
Do you want him here,
or do you not want him here?

1100
01:08:46.960 --> 01:08:49.645
Honestly, I don't give a rat's ass
about that man. That's your hero.

1101
01:08:49.720 --> 01:08:52.644
Let's take these bastards
and stick them down into Alabama River

1102
01:08:52.720 --> 01:08:53.960
and never see them again.

1103
01:08:54.040 --> 01:08:55.485
James, you are so off-base with this.

1104
01:08:55.560 --> 01:08:57.324
All this nonsense.
This ain't what SNCC is about.

1105
01:08:57.400 --> 01:08:58.481
Don't make me out to be
the bad guy here, John.

1106
01:08:58.560 --> 01:09:00.324
I'm not! You're the one playing me small.

1107
01:09:00.400 --> 01:09:01.970
- Don't demonize me...
- (OVERLAPPING ARGUMENT)

1108
01:09:02.400 --> 01:09:04.528
You're mad because they called him in.

1109
01:09:05.840 --> 01:09:07.922
We were here first.
And they called him in.

1110
01:09:08.000 --> 01:09:10.480
I get it. I understand that.

1111
01:09:10.560 --> 01:09:14.007
But if we are really
and truly for the people,

1112
01:09:14.080 --> 01:09:16.401
and the people of Selma chose him,

1113
01:09:17.880 --> 01:09:19.848
well, then the people have spoken.

1114
01:09:21.840 --> 01:09:24.525
And if they want to march,
then I'm marching with them.

1115
01:09:28.240 --> 01:09:29.765
Then, brother,

1116
01:09:30.920 --> 01:09:33.241
you're marching as John Lewis.

1117
01:09:34.040 --> 01:09:35.804
Not as part of SNCC.

1118
01:09:37.760 --> 01:09:39.762
It's been voted on and decided.

1119
01:09:40.680 --> 01:09:44.685
For this march, you're on your own
with De Lawd and his disciples.

1120
01:10:11.600 --> 01:10:13.648
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

1121
01:10:15.800 --> 01:10:17.643
VIVIAN: Short man wins.
Short man wins.

1122
01:10:18.280 --> 01:10:19.770
Short man wins.

1123
01:10:21.400 --> 01:10:22.606
All right.

1124
01:10:24.640 --> 01:10:26.802
All right. Who got it?

1125
01:10:28.480 --> 01:10:30.005
It's on you, Hosea.

1126
01:10:30.120 --> 01:10:31.804
WILLIAMS: You ready, young blood?
You ready?

1127
01:10:32.800 --> 01:10:35.007
- All right. Let's do this.
- All right.

1128
01:10:39.800 --> 01:10:42.565
REED: <i>About 525 Negroes
had left Brown's Chapel</i>

1129
01:10:42.640 --> 01:10:46.167
<i>and walked six blocks to cross
Pettus Bridge and the Alabama River.</i>

1130
01:11:01.880 --> 01:11:03.848
There were young and old,

1131
01:11:03.920 --> 01:11:07.891
and they carried an assortment of packs,
bed rolls and lunch sacks.

1132
01:12:21.160 --> 01:12:25.210
<i>The troopers were waiting
300 yards beyond the end of the bridge.</i>

1133
01:12:26.160 --> 01:12:28.731
<i>Behind the troopers
were dozens of possemen,</i>

1134
01:12:29.400 --> 01:12:31.482
<i>15 of them on horses,</i>

1135
01:12:31.560 --> 01:12:34.689
<i>and perhaps 100 white spectators.</i>

1136
01:12:44.760 --> 01:12:46.489
Can you swim?

1137
01:12:47.800 --> 01:12:51.361
Not many swimming pools for
black folk where I come from.

1138
01:12:52.400 --> 01:12:54.050
Yeah.

1139
01:13:10.960 --> 01:13:12.883
(REPORTERS CHATTERING
INDISTINCTLY)

1140
01:13:12.960 --> 01:13:14.325
(CAMERAS CLICKING)

1141
01:13:21.680 --> 01:13:23.808
<i>Andy, it's Bayard. Everybody there?</i>

1142
01:13:24.080 --> 01:13:25.081
Yes.

1143
01:13:25.160 --> 01:13:26.366
BAYARD: <i>Turn on CBS right now, Andy.</i>

1144
01:13:26.440 --> 01:13:27.680
Right now. You have a TV there?

1145
01:13:27.960 --> 01:13:29.849
- Yes. Now?
- Right now!

1146
01:13:30.160 --> 01:13:31.924
Turn on the television set.

1147
01:13:32.840 --> 01:13:34.569
ANNOUNCER ON TV: <i>We interrupt
this program to bring you</i>

1148
01:13:34.680 --> 01:13:37.001
<i>a special bulletin from CBS News.</i>

1149
01:13:52.720 --> 01:13:55.200
Give 'em two minutes. Stand right there.

1150
01:13:55.280 --> 01:13:56.691
We're ready.

1151
01:14:09.960 --> 01:14:11.962
<i>This is an unlawful assembly.</i>

1152
01:14:12.040 --> 01:14:14.361
<i>You have two minutes to disperse.</i>

1153
01:14:14.440 --> 01:14:17.284
<i>Go home or go to your church.</i>

1154
01:14:17.360 --> 01:14:20.443
<i>This march will not continue.</i>

1155
01:14:21.000 --> 01:14:22.809
Two minutes.

1156
01:14:26.120 --> 01:14:28.805
May I have a word with the Major?

1157
01:14:31.200 --> 01:14:33.043
<i>There's no word to be had.</i>

1158
01:14:35.440 --> 01:14:37.363
Major Cloud, may we speak with you?

1159
01:14:50.480 --> 01:14:52.084
<i>Troopers, advance!</i>

1160
01:14:52.640 --> 01:14:53.641
(GUNSHOT)

1161
01:14:53.960 --> 01:14:55.371
(TROOPERS YELLING)

1162
01:15:01.800 --> 01:15:03.040
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1163
01:15:05.360 --> 01:15:06.566
(PEOPLE SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

1164
01:15:07.760 --> 01:15:10.411
Seventy million people are watching this.

1165
01:15:10.480 --> 01:15:12.403
REED: <i>The first 10 or 20 Negroes</i>

1166
01:15:12.480 --> 01:15:14.084
<i>were swept to the ground screaming,</i>

1167
01:15:14.160 --> 01:15:15.446
<i>arms and legs flying,</i>

1168
01:15:15.520 --> 01:15:18.410
<i>packs and bags went skittering
across the grassy divider.</i>

1169
01:15:19.320 --> 01:15:20.606
(GUNFIRE)

1170
01:15:21.800 --> 01:15:23.450
(ALL SCREAMING)

1171
01:15:28.760 --> 01:15:30.046
(GROANING)

1172
01:15:33.360 --> 01:15:35.806
REED: <i>Those still on their feet retreated.</i>

1173
01:15:35.880 --> 01:15:37.928
<i>A cheer went up
from the white spectators</i>

1174
01:15:38.000 --> 01:15:39.604
<i>lining the south side of the highway.</i>

1175
01:15:39.840 --> 01:15:41.251
(ALL SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

1176
01:15:44.960 --> 01:15:46.371
- (COUGHING)
- Come on.

1177
01:15:47.640 --> 01:15:49.005
You gotta come on.

1178
01:15:49.080 --> 01:15:50.206
MAN: Please, don't...

1179
01:15:51.800 --> 01:15:53.245
REED: <i>The troopers continued pushing,</i>

1180
01:15:53.360 --> 01:15:56.489
<i>using both the force of their bodies
and the prodding of their nightsticks.</i>

1181
01:16:00.480 --> 01:16:01.527
(GROANS)

1182
01:16:03.200 --> 01:16:05.851
(ALL CLAMORING)

1183
01:16:09.200 --> 01:16:10.281
(GUNSHOT)

1184
01:16:11.080 --> 01:16:14.766
REED: <i>Suddenly, there was
a sharp sound, like a gunshot,</i>

1185
01:16:14.880 --> 01:16:19.010
<i>and a gray cloud spewed over
the troopers and the Negroes.</i>

1186
01:16:19.080 --> 01:16:21.560
<i>But before the cloud hid it all,</i>

1187
01:16:21.680 --> 01:16:25.844
there were several seconds
of unobstructed view.

1188
01:16:25.920 --> 01:16:26.967
(CLEARS THROAT)

1189
01:16:39.280 --> 01:16:40.281
(YELLING)

1190
01:16:46.200 --> 01:16:48.168
REED: <i>Fifteen or 20 nightsticks</i>

1191
01:16:48.240 --> 01:16:50.288
<i>could be seen through the gas,</i>

1192
01:16:50.360 --> 01:16:53.170
<i>flailing at the heads of the marchers.</i>

1193
01:16:53.440 --> 01:16:54.487
Ahhh!

1194
01:16:54.560 --> 01:16:56.005
REED: <i>The Negroes cried out</i>

1195
01:16:56.080 --> 01:16:57.730
<i>as they crowded together for protection,</i>

1196
01:16:57.840 --> 01:17:00.002
<i>and the whites on the sidelines
whooped and cheered.</i>

1197
01:17:12.800 --> 01:17:15.485
<i>From the hospital
came reports of victims</i>

1198
01:17:15.560 --> 01:17:19.804
<i>suffering fractures of ribs,
heads, arms and legs.</i>

1199
01:17:19.880 --> 01:17:21.882
<i>And Negro leader John Lewis,</i>

1200
01:17:21.960 --> 01:17:24.088
<i>despite injury from
a possible skull fracture,</i>

1201
01:17:24.200 --> 01:17:28.330
<i>led the marchers back to the chapel
after the encounter with officers.</i>

1202
01:17:29.240 --> 01:17:30.685
Help!

1203
01:17:31.200 --> 01:17:32.201
Help!

1204
01:17:36.960 --> 01:17:40.851
<i>He said, "I don't see
how President Johnson</i>

1205
01:17:40.920 --> 01:17:42.331
<i>"can send troops to Vietnam</i>

1206
01:17:42.600 --> 01:17:46.366
"and can't send troops
to Selma, Alabama."

1207
01:17:46.440 --> 01:17:50.570
To which the Negroes present
roared their approval.

1208
01:17:51.240 --> 01:17:53.402
(GOSPEL MUSIC PLAYING)

1209
01:18:09.840 --> 01:18:11.729
(INAUDIBLE)

1210
01:18:32.720 --> 01:18:35.166
MAN: Gerry! Gerry, come with us!
Come with us!

1211
01:18:35.240 --> 01:18:36.571
We need your gun, man!

1212
01:18:36.640 --> 01:18:37.971
GERRY: I can't walk!

1213
01:18:38.040 --> 01:18:40.646
MAN: Come with us. We know you got
them guns in the shed, Gerry.

1214
01:18:40.720 --> 01:18:43.087
Hey, hey, hey, what you need guns for?

1215
01:18:43.160 --> 01:18:44.844
The Bible says,
"An eye for an eye," Reverend.

1216
01:18:44.920 --> 01:18:46.490
- Yeah?
- I'm sick of this shit!

1217
01:18:46.560 --> 01:18:48.642
How many guns
you think they got down there?

1218
01:18:48.720 --> 01:18:50.609
That's an entire army down there.

1219
01:18:50.680 --> 01:18:52.967
What you got? A couple of .32s? A .38?

1220
01:18:53.080 --> 01:18:54.411
Maybe a couple
of old scatterguns? What?

1221
01:18:54.480 --> 01:18:57.006
I got enough to kill a couple
of them crackers, that's what I got!

1222
01:18:57.080 --> 01:19:00.368
And how many of us you think
they gonna kill in retaliation?

1223
01:19:00.440 --> 01:19:03.569
With their 12-gauge pump-actions,
their Colt automatics,

1224
01:19:03.640 --> 01:19:05.961
their Remingtons, their helicopters,
their tanks!

1225
01:19:06.840 --> 01:19:10.367
We won't win that way,
and I ain't talking about the Bible.

1226
01:19:10.440 --> 01:19:12.169
I ain't talking what's right by God.

1227
01:19:12.240 --> 01:19:14.766
I am talking facts. Cold, hard facts!

1228
01:19:14.840 --> 01:19:19.209
Now, you take two of them,
and they take 10 of us.

1229
01:19:19.280 --> 01:19:22.887
No. We have to win another way.

1230
01:19:24.280 --> 01:19:26.442
ANNOUNCER: (ON TV) <i>...to our
regularly scheduled program.</i>

1231
01:19:34.120 --> 01:19:36.168
We're going back to the bridge.

1232
01:19:39.640 --> 01:19:43.201
We're going to finish this,
we promise you that, Ms. Amelia.

1233
01:19:46.400 --> 01:19:48.243
We go again.

1234
01:19:50.480 --> 01:19:51.481
(REPORTERS CLAMORING)

1235
01:19:51.560 --> 01:19:52.607
(CAMERAS CLICKING)

1236
01:19:53.360 --> 01:19:56.091
MALE REPORTER: Dr. King!
Can we get a statement, sir?

1237
01:19:56.160 --> 01:19:57.400
Dr. King! Morning, Doctor.

1238
01:19:57.520 --> 01:19:58.965
Can we get a statement, please?

1239
01:19:59.040 --> 01:20:00.451
- KING: Morning.
- Morning.

1240
01:20:01.920 --> 01:20:07.290
While rageful violence continues
towards the unarmed people of Selma,

1241
01:20:07.640 --> 01:20:13.409
while they are assaulted with tear gas
and batons like an enemy in a war,

1242
01:20:13.480 --> 01:20:17.041
no citizen of this country
can call themselves blameless,

1243
01:20:17.120 --> 01:20:20.806
for we all bear a responsibility
for our fellow man.

1244
01:20:21.440 --> 01:20:24.444
I am appealing to
men and women of God

1245
01:20:24.520 --> 01:20:26.522
and goodwill everywhere,

1246
01:20:26.600 --> 01:20:28.921
white, black and otherwise.

1247
01:20:29.000 --> 01:20:34.769
If you believe all are created equal,
come to Selma.

1248
01:20:34.840 --> 01:20:39.289
Join us. Join our march against injustice
and inhumanity.

1249
01:20:40.200 --> 01:20:41.850
We need you to stand with us.

1250
01:20:44.560 --> 01:20:47.484
GRAY: <i>Judge Johnson,
Dr. King's call-to-action</i>

1251
01:20:47.560 --> 01:20:49.289
<i>was nationally televised.</i>

1252
01:20:50.680 --> 01:20:52.808
<i>We've seen hundreds of people
travel across the country</i>

1253
01:20:52.880 --> 01:20:54.644
<i>to attend tomorrow's march,</i>

1254
01:20:54.720 --> 01:20:58.805
<i>mostly white,
mostly clergy of some kind.</i>

1255
01:21:00.320 --> 01:21:03.529
The SCLC is seeking
a federal court order

1256
01:21:03.600 --> 01:21:06.968
enjoining the state authorities
from interfering with the next march.

1257
01:21:08.160 --> 01:21:10.527
You're asking me to overturn
the Governor's mandate

1258
01:21:10.600 --> 01:21:12.602
and to do so without a hearing,

1259
01:21:12.720 --> 01:21:13.960
but it's not going to happen at all

1260
01:21:14.720 --> 01:21:16.051
without a proper proceeding.

1261
01:21:16.120 --> 01:21:19.090
Dr. King is in position
to lead tomorrow's march, Judge.

1262
01:21:19.160 --> 01:21:23.165
Understood, but you will have
your day in court on Thursday, Mr. Gray.

1263
01:21:23.240 --> 01:21:26.050
Meanwhile, there will be
no march tomorrow.

1264
01:21:26.120 --> 01:21:28.646
I will not oppose Wallace
against protocol.

1265
01:21:29.960 --> 01:21:32.884
"Thousands head south
in moral crusade."

1266
01:21:36.720 --> 01:21:38.484
WHITE: The SCLC
already filed an appeal

1267
01:21:38.560 --> 01:21:40.927
against Wallace's orders this morning.

1268
01:21:43.560 --> 01:21:45.528
You want my advice, Mr. President?

1269
01:21:45.920 --> 01:21:47.445
You have to ask?

1270
01:21:47.680 --> 01:21:50.524
Give King the march to Montgomery.

1271
01:21:52.400 --> 01:21:55.563
Do that, and then Selma's over.

1272
01:21:57.000 --> 01:21:58.161
Then you're back in control.

1273
01:21:58.320 --> 01:22:00.322
In control of what?

1274
01:22:00.400 --> 01:22:02.289
Another civil war?

1275
01:22:02.360 --> 01:22:04.010
This ain't about the goddamn march.

1276
01:22:04.080 --> 01:22:05.809
You think he cares about the march?

1277
01:22:05.880 --> 01:22:08.486
He wants the law changed, now.

1278
01:22:09.160 --> 01:22:10.571
I've got Congress
calling me by the dozens.

1279
01:22:10.640 --> 01:22:13.120
I've got picketing that gets
bigger and bigger every day.

1280
01:22:13.240 --> 01:22:15.811
He tugs on their goddamn
white liberal conscience.

1281
01:22:16.280 --> 01:22:19.841
Every march pulls 'em. Especially when
people are getting beat up in the streets.

1282
01:22:23.760 --> 01:22:26.206
These pictures are going
around the world, Lee.

1283
01:22:26.600 --> 01:22:28.523
I understand, Mr. President.

1284
01:22:28.600 --> 01:22:30.204
All the more reason to act now.

1285
01:22:30.280 --> 01:22:31.327
I'm gonna act now.

1286
01:22:32.280 --> 01:22:34.886
You tell Wallace
and those backwater hicks

1287
01:22:34.960 --> 01:22:37.042
I don't want to see
any more of this horseshit.

1288
01:22:37.120 --> 01:22:40.249
And you tell King he best not march,
you hear me?

1289
01:22:40.320 --> 01:22:43.767
Either King stops and Wallace stops,

1290
01:22:43.840 --> 01:22:45.808
or I'll stop 'em both.

1291
01:22:45.960 --> 01:22:49.407
I'm here on the President's order
to try and make this work.

1292
01:22:50.680 --> 01:22:52.205
Please work with me.

1293
01:22:53.480 --> 01:22:55.323
So we give up the march and you...

1294
01:22:56.360 --> 01:22:57.725
You give what?

1295
01:22:58.680 --> 01:23:00.205
We asked for federal protection.

1296
01:23:00.280 --> 01:23:01.770
And with no disrespect,

1297
01:23:01.840 --> 01:23:03.330
but when the Assistant Attorney General

1298
01:23:03.400 --> 01:23:05.482
is the highest-ranking
federal official in Selma,

1299
01:23:05.560 --> 01:23:07.767
we have our answer.

1300
01:23:07.840 --> 01:23:09.126
And it's not the one we want.

1301
01:23:09.200 --> 01:23:13.922
Might I suggest that you
speak with Governor Wallace

1302
01:23:14.000 --> 01:23:16.606
and Sheriff Clark
and urge them against violence

1303
01:23:16.720 --> 01:23:18.484
instead of trying to persuade us

1304
01:23:18.560 --> 01:23:20.369
not to have a peaceful protest?

1305
01:23:26.240 --> 01:23:28.163
Maybe we can make a deal.

1306
01:23:29.440 --> 01:23:31.090
What if I

1307
01:23:31.760 --> 01:23:36.129
could assure you that the administration
would endorse a later march

1308
01:23:37.160 --> 01:23:38.525
if tomorrow is called off?

1309
01:23:40.240 --> 01:23:44.245
You know what?
He's closer than you may think

1310
01:23:44.600 --> 01:23:46.841
to coming around on this issue.

1311
01:23:48.160 --> 01:23:50.686
I believe this compromise
might be agreeable.

1312
01:23:50.760 --> 01:23:52.000
KING: Mr. Doar?

1313
01:23:53.040 --> 01:23:57.568
Thousands have gathered here
to demonstrate their dignity.

1314
01:23:59.240 --> 01:24:01.129
I don't want to challenge Judge Johnson.

1315
01:24:01.200 --> 01:24:03.009
I don't want to go against the President.

1316
01:24:03.080 --> 01:24:04.320
I don't want any of this.

1317
01:24:05.240 --> 01:24:08.005
The President could stop this
with a stroke of his pen.

1318
01:24:08.080 --> 01:24:10.208
He chooses not to.

1319
01:24:10.280 --> 01:24:12.760
The decision is with your side, sir,

1320
01:24:13.800 --> 01:24:14.961
not ours.

1321
01:24:17.000 --> 01:24:18.809
(BLUES MUSIC PLAYING)

1322
01:24:24.320 --> 01:24:26.084
Good to see you, Father.
Good to see you.

1323
01:24:26.160 --> 01:24:27.525
Thank you for coming.
Thank you for coming out.

1324
01:24:27.600 --> 01:24:29.364
Hello, sister. Good to
see you this afternoon.

1325
01:24:30.080 --> 01:24:33.084
Oh. Oh... You came.

1326
01:24:33.160 --> 01:24:35.401
You called and we came, my friend.

1327
01:24:35.480 --> 01:24:36.845
You are not alone, my friend.

1328
01:24:36.920 --> 01:24:38.081
Welcome, welcome.

1329
01:24:38.160 --> 01:24:39.321
- Hi, what's your name?
- Susan.

1330
01:24:39.720 --> 01:24:41.404
Hi, I'm Viola. Welcome to Selma.

1331
01:24:42.040 --> 01:24:44.327
- Yes, ma'am, I'm good. How are you?
- Fine, thank you.

1332
01:24:44.400 --> 01:24:46.004
What is your name
and where are you from, sir?

1333
01:24:46.080 --> 01:24:48.890
My name is James Reeb.
I've come from Boston.

1334
01:24:48.960 --> 01:24:52.282
Tell me, why have you
traveled here, Mr. Reeb?

1335
01:24:52.920 --> 01:24:56.720
I heard about the attack
of innocent people

1336
01:24:56.800 --> 01:24:58.165
who just want their rights,

1337
01:24:58.480 --> 01:25:03.008
and I couldn't just stand by
when Dr. King put out that call to clergy.

1338
01:25:03.520 --> 01:25:04.601
I couldn't.

1339
01:25:04.920 --> 01:25:07.002
<i>The President doesn't
want us to march today.</i>

1340
01:25:07.120 --> 01:25:08.246
(CROWD CHEERS)

1341
01:25:08.320 --> 01:25:10.288
<i>The courts don't want us to march.</i>

1342
01:25:10.760 --> 01:25:11.761
<i>But we must march.</i>

1343
01:25:11.840 --> 01:25:12.841
ALL: Yeah!

1344
01:25:12.960 --> 01:25:14.689
<i>- We must stand up.</i>
- ALL: Yeah!

1345
01:25:14.760 --> 01:25:18.606
<i>We must make a massive demonstration
of our moral certainty.</i>

1346
01:25:19.120 --> 01:25:20.645
(CROWD CHEERING)

1347
01:25:22.320 --> 01:25:26.041
<i>I'm so glad we're here together today.</i>

1348
01:25:26.320 --> 01:25:28.607
<i>I thank you for standing up.</i>

1349
01:25:29.000 --> 01:25:32.049
<i>For we shall be victorious in our quest.</i>

1350
01:25:32.120 --> 01:25:35.090
<i>We shall cross the finish line
hand in hand.</i>

1351
01:25:36.520 --> 01:25:39.046
<i>For we shall overcome.</i>

1352
01:25:39.600 --> 01:25:40.647
<i>All right.</i>

1353
01:25:40.720 --> 01:25:42.051
(APPLAUSE)

1354
01:26:02.520 --> 01:26:04.602
(FOLK MUSIC PLAYING)

1355
01:27:17.800 --> 01:27:20.485
<i>Troopers, withdraw!</i>

1356
01:27:40.680 --> 01:27:42.921
(APPLAUSE)

1357
01:29:46.600 --> 01:29:48.602
My point is,
after what happened the last time,

1358
01:29:48.680 --> 01:29:50.808
if it don't feel right, we don't do it.
That's my point.

1359
01:29:50.880 --> 01:29:52.723
We've been going round
and round on this for hours,

1360
01:29:52.800 --> 01:29:54.325
and nothing's gonna change the fact that

1361
01:29:54.400 --> 01:29:56.289
it was Doc's decision
and we have to support him.

1362
01:29:56.360 --> 01:29:57.930
NASH: This is a movement
of many, not of one.

1363
01:29:58.000 --> 01:29:59.570
So any choice we make
has to be right for many.

1364
01:29:59.640 --> 01:30:02.166
Come on, Diane. Now, you know
that's not what I meant by that, all right?

1365
01:30:02.240 --> 01:30:04.527
People are angry, Dr. King.

1366
01:30:05.040 --> 01:30:09.887
Angry. They went back to that bridge
because they were hot about Sunday.

1367
01:30:09.960 --> 01:30:11.883
That was our moment out there today.

1368
01:30:11.960 --> 01:30:13.246
And you threw it away.

1369
01:30:13.880 --> 01:30:16.326
They could've sealed off
the road behind us.

1370
01:30:16.400 --> 01:30:20.121
No food, water, no kind of
support allowed through.

1371
01:30:21.120 --> 01:30:22.610
We wouldn't have made 10 miles.

1372
01:30:22.680 --> 01:30:24.045
You saying this was a trap?

1373
01:30:24.280 --> 01:30:25.850
(SIGHS)

1374
01:30:27.480 --> 01:30:28.811
I don't know what it was.

1375
01:30:29.520 --> 01:30:31.727
That was no trap!

1376
01:30:31.800 --> 01:30:33.689
You know why they
opened up the road to us?

1377
01:30:34.120 --> 01:30:36.805
Because all them nice,
respectable white folks

1378
01:30:36.880 --> 01:30:38.928
was with us, and we
should've capitalized on that.

1379
01:30:39.000 --> 01:30:41.287
Because they're not gonna be
around here for long. They never are!

1380
01:30:41.360 --> 01:30:43.601
It was Martin's call. It's done.

1381
01:30:43.680 --> 01:30:46.763
- He made the wrong goddamn call!
- Hey, watch your mouth, young man!

1382
01:30:46.840 --> 01:30:49.207
Two days ago,
you didn't wanna march at all.

1383
01:30:49.280 --> 01:30:52.090
And now you're mad because
it didn't go the way you planned?

1384
01:30:52.160 --> 01:30:53.889
BEVEL: Calm down, brother.

1385
01:30:57.880 --> 01:30:59.370
Now, what happened out there today?

1386
01:30:59.440 --> 01:31:01.408
You gotta tell us something. Please.

1387
01:31:09.080 --> 01:31:11.811
I'd rather people be upset and hate me

1388
01:31:11.880 --> 01:31:14.884
than be bleeding or dead.

1389
01:31:41.160 --> 01:31:42.650
(SIGHS)

1390
01:32:09.840 --> 01:32:12.525
KING: <i>My dearest Corrie,</i>

1391
01:32:14.520 --> 01:32:16.602
<i>at a time when I need you,</i>

1392
01:32:17.600 --> 01:32:19.568
<i>I cannot call you.</i>

1393
01:32:21.080 --> 01:32:25.802
<i>And I have done this to myself, to us.</i>

1394
01:32:29.400 --> 01:32:31.482
<i>At this late hour,</i>

1395
01:32:32.680 --> 01:32:35.251
<i>my thoughts are of you</i>

1396
01:32:35.360 --> 01:32:38.682
<i>and all you have sacrificed
for this struggle.</i>

1397
01:32:40.360 --> 01:32:43.330
<i>So many have sacrificed.</i>

1398
01:32:44.400 --> 01:32:46.846
<i>So many have been lost.</i>

1399
01:32:48.160 --> 01:32:51.721
<i>I wonder how many must we lose.</i>

1400
01:32:55.640 --> 01:33:00.771
<i>I pray for discernment and guidance
as we journey on.</i>

1401
01:33:02.360 --> 01:33:06.922
<i>I pray, too, that I can justify
the faith you once had in me.</i>

1402
01:33:09.600 --> 01:33:16.245
<i>I, too, often feel that heavy fog
you spoke of, Corrie.</i>

1403
01:33:18.760 --> 01:33:23.766
<i>Only you and our family clears the haze.</i>

1404
01:33:26.160 --> 01:33:29.050
<i>Love, Martin.</i>

1405
01:33:31.880 --> 01:33:33.120
MAN: <i>He betrayed trust.</i>

1406
01:33:33.600 --> 01:33:36.763
He called, we came,
and he didn't fulfill his own call.

1407
01:33:36.880 --> 01:33:39.008
Yeah, but sometimes
it's not that clear-cut.

1408
01:33:39.080 --> 01:33:41.367
Sometimes it's instinctual.

1409
01:33:42.320 --> 01:33:44.004
Like when you're preaching,

1410
01:33:44.680 --> 01:33:46.409
and you're just flying.

1411
01:33:47.680 --> 01:33:50.843
You know, you're not on the notes.
You're not on memory.

1412
01:33:50.920 --> 01:33:55.403
You're tapped into what's higher,
what's true.

1413
01:33:56.280 --> 01:33:57.611
God is guiding you.

1414
01:33:59.240 --> 01:34:01.129
I've known that feeling.

1415
01:34:01.200 --> 01:34:02.486
It's rare, but I've known it.

1416
01:34:02.600 --> 01:34:03.840
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

1417
01:34:05.960 --> 01:34:09.760
I think that's what happened to Dr. King
up there on the bridge today.

1418
01:34:09.840 --> 01:34:12.320
He kneeled down,
prayed to God and got an answer.

1419
01:34:12.400 --> 01:34:15.290
And he was brave enough
to follow that answer,

1420
01:34:15.360 --> 01:34:18.250
and I, for one, don't fault him for it.

1421
01:34:18.320 --> 01:34:21.210
- Except he owes me a bus ticket home.
- (CHUCKLES)

1422
01:34:21.280 --> 01:34:22.645
MAN 1: You know what
I hate more than niggers?

1423
01:34:22.760 --> 01:34:24.091
MAN 2: What's that?

1424
01:34:24.720 --> 01:34:25.846
White niggers.

1425
01:34:26.760 --> 01:34:28.330
Look, we don't want trouble, okay?

1426
01:34:28.400 --> 01:34:30.129
MAN 1: No, you came here
stirrin' trouble.

1427
01:34:38.920 --> 01:34:40.206
(GROANING)

1428
01:34:40.320 --> 01:34:41.367
(GRUNTS)

1429
01:34:47.520 --> 01:34:48.601
Doc,

1430
01:34:50.480 --> 01:34:51.845
someone's been hurt.

1431
01:34:54.400 --> 01:34:56.004
(GROANING)

1432
01:34:56.600 --> 01:34:59.649
A priest, from Boston.

1433
01:35:01.200 --> 01:35:02.361
<i>White.</i>

1434
01:35:03.640 --> 01:35:08.123
Now you know what being a nigger
around here feels like, boy.

1435
01:35:08.640 --> 01:35:10.927
Hurt? How?

1436
01:35:17.800 --> 01:35:18.926
Dead.

1437
01:35:19.080 --> 01:35:20.286
(GASPS)

1438
01:35:34.760 --> 01:35:36.330
I need a phone!

1439
01:35:37.640 --> 01:35:41.531
Chicago, Detroit, Boston, I don't care.

1440
01:35:41.600 --> 01:35:43.728
Hell, you got 2,000 people
marching up in Harlem.

1441
01:35:43.840 --> 01:35:45.126
Well, good for you.

1442
01:35:45.200 --> 01:35:48.010
<i>But when you have people
come inside the White House?</i>

1443
01:35:48.080 --> 01:35:50.765
Inside the White House! On a tour?

1444
01:35:51.120 --> 01:35:52.406
<i>They just sat down, Martin.</i>

1445
01:35:52.480 --> 01:35:54.130
They sat down in the main corridor,

1446
01:35:54.200 --> 01:35:56.441
started singin' and shoutin'.
Well, I won't have it!

1447
01:35:56.560 --> 01:35:57.971
I cannot stop people from expressing...

1448
01:35:58.040 --> 01:35:59.724
You can! You can stop them.

1449
01:35:59.800 --> 01:36:03.691
No, you can stop it.
You, sir, can do more.

1450
01:36:03.760 --> 01:36:06.923
Now I'm glad to hear that you called
Reverend Reeb's widow, sir.

1451
01:36:07.000 --> 01:36:08.968
That is very fine, and it is right.

1452
01:36:09.040 --> 01:36:11.008
<i>I only wish that
Jimmie Lee Jackson's family</i>

1453
01:36:11.080 --> 01:36:13.731
would have received the same
consideration from their President.

1454
01:36:13.800 --> 01:36:15.802
Don't you lay your guilt at my door.

1455
01:36:15.880 --> 01:36:17.291
You're the one choosing to send

1456
01:36:17.360 --> 01:36:20.011
people out to slaughter
when we told you there was trouble.

1457
01:36:20.080 --> 01:36:21.286
<i>We won't sit idle</i>

1458
01:36:21.360 --> 01:36:24.091
while you wait another year or two
to send this bill up at your leisure.

1459
01:36:24.160 --> 01:36:26.527
<i>That should be clear by now.</i>

1460
01:36:26.600 --> 01:36:30.525
<i>We will continue to demonstrate
until you take action, sir.</i>

1461
01:36:30.600 --> 01:36:32.443
<i>And if our President
won't protect our rights,</i>

1462
01:36:32.520 --> 01:36:33.885
<i>we will take this fight to court.</i>

1463
01:36:34.960 --> 01:36:37.247
You know, I'm... I'm trying here.

1464
01:36:37.320 --> 01:36:39.084
We're getting close
to figuring something out

1465
01:36:39.160 --> 01:36:41.970
on this voting thing,
but I will not have this!

1466
01:36:43.320 --> 01:36:45.641
<i>This bill has been
almost impossible to craft,</i>

1467
01:36:45.720 --> 01:36:47.051
<i>you hear me?</i>

1468
01:36:47.120 --> 01:36:50.522
<i>You think you're jugglin', Martin?
I'm jugglin', too.</i>

1469
01:36:52.280 --> 01:36:54.408
I am a preacher from Atlanta.

1470
01:36:54.800 --> 01:36:58.600
You are the man who won the presidency
of the world's most powerful nation

1471
01:36:58.680 --> 01:37:02.002
<i>by the greatest landslide
in history four months ago.</i>

1472
01:37:02.360 --> 01:37:03.600
<i>And you are the man</i>

1473
01:37:03.680 --> 01:37:07.685
dismantling your own legacy
with each passing day.

1474
01:37:09.280 --> 01:37:11.362
<i>No one will remember
the Civil Rights Act.</i>

1475
01:37:11.880 --> 01:37:14.486
But they will remember
the standoff in Selma

1476
01:37:14.560 --> 01:37:17.291
when you never even
set foot in this state.

1477
01:37:17.360 --> 01:37:20.921
<i>They will remember you saying,
"Wait," and "I can't,"</i>

1478
01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:24.402
unless you act, sir.

1479
01:37:36.240 --> 01:37:38.129
- KING: Evenin'.
- Evenin'.

1480
01:37:39.280 --> 01:37:41.567
(MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO)

1481
01:37:54.280 --> 01:37:56.567
I wanted to speak privately.

1482
01:37:57.520 --> 01:38:00.364
I know there's been trouble
with the group,

1483
01:38:00.440 --> 01:38:02.488
and I apologize that our efforts

1484
01:38:02.560 --> 01:38:04.801
have caused a rift between y'all.

1485
01:38:06.440 --> 01:38:08.044
That's a painful thing, I know,

1486
01:38:08.120 --> 01:38:10.088
and I'm truly sorry it's happened.

1487
01:38:11.560 --> 01:38:14.564
Yeah, painful.

1488
01:38:16.800 --> 01:38:18.006
(SIGHS)

1489
01:38:20.400 --> 01:38:22.368
LBJ is not moving, John.

1490
01:38:24.360 --> 01:38:26.840
I thought he would,
but our efforts are not working,

1491
01:38:26.960 --> 01:38:29.327
and I can't risk another march
with people getting killed

1492
01:38:29.400 --> 01:38:31.164
when it's not working. I won't do it.

1493
01:38:32.280 --> 01:38:35.363
We need voting, not marching.
You know that.

1494
01:38:36.160 --> 01:38:40.609
We have to move beyond these protests
to some real political power.

1495
01:38:40.680 --> 01:38:43.001
This can't go on forever like this.

1496
01:38:44.680 --> 01:38:46.682
I can't go on like this.

1497
01:38:56.840 --> 01:38:58.046
(SIGHS)

1498
01:39:02.480 --> 01:39:04.050
When I was...

1499
01:39:06.000 --> 01:39:09.925
When I was working with SNCC
on the Freedom Rides,

1500
01:39:12.600 --> 01:39:16.082
the Montgomery bus
reached the city limits.

1501
01:39:17.760 --> 01:39:20.206
We got off. And out of nowhere,

1502
01:39:21.600 --> 01:39:25.571
from all directions, they came.

1503
01:39:28.280 --> 01:39:31.568
There was men, women.

1504
01:39:33.680 --> 01:39:35.125
Kids, too.

1505
01:39:38.240 --> 01:39:42.609
They had just about every
makeshift weapon you could think of.

1506
01:39:42.680 --> 01:39:45.206
I mean, bats, bricks,

1507
01:39:46.680 --> 01:39:50.241
tire irons, pipes.

1508
01:39:54.040 --> 01:39:55.769
I remember...

1509
01:39:57.200 --> 01:40:01.364
I remember this little girl
just clawing her nails

1510
01:40:01.440 --> 01:40:05.365
into the side of my friend Jessie's face

1511
01:40:05.440 --> 01:40:09.604
while her daddy... Her daddy
beat him with an ax handle.

1512
01:40:12.680 --> 01:40:14.489
Jessie was unconscious,

1513
01:40:14.560 --> 01:40:17.484
and they just kept beating on him
and beating on him.

1514
01:40:22.040 --> 01:40:24.850
I must've passed out
on the asphalt somewhere.

1515
01:40:29.000 --> 01:40:34.769
Next day, I found myself patched up
and sitting in a church.

1516
01:40:35.600 --> 01:40:38.888
I could barely hold my head up,
but I needed to be there.

1517
01:40:41.080 --> 01:40:43.162
You were gonna be speaking.

1518
01:40:44.040 --> 01:40:46.202
And I needed to hear you.

1519
01:40:48.880 --> 01:40:51.804
And I was feeling down,
but you got up there.

1520
01:40:54.400 --> 01:40:55.970
You remember that day at all?

1521
01:40:56.520 --> 01:40:57.601
(KING SIGHS)

1522
01:40:57.680 --> 01:41:00.490
I don't think we remember it
the same way.

1523
01:41:02.000 --> 01:41:03.604
What'd I say, John?

1524
01:41:04.960 --> 01:41:07.327
I'm about to tell you right now.

1525
01:41:08.600 --> 01:41:10.489
And I hope you hear me.

1526
01:41:12.800 --> 01:41:15.246
You said that we would triumph.

1527
01:41:16.040 --> 01:41:19.647
That we would triumph
because there could be no other way.

1528
01:41:23.720 --> 01:41:25.643
And you know what else you said?

1529
01:41:30.680 --> 01:41:31.727
You said,

1530
01:41:32.720 --> 01:41:34.165
"Fear not.

1531
01:41:35.560 --> 01:41:38.564
"We've come too far to turn back now."

1532
01:41:50.600 --> 01:41:52.284
KING: I feel good about where we are.

1533
01:41:52.360 --> 01:41:54.089
We have a strong case.

1534
01:41:54.160 --> 01:41:55.491
- We can do this.
- Right.

1535
01:41:56.080 --> 01:41:59.880
KING: Now, Ms. Cooper
and Ms. Boynton are here,

1536
01:41:59.960 --> 01:42:01.689
- and they need to be ready.
- LEWIS: Mmm-hmm.

1537
01:42:03.600 --> 01:42:05.648
KING: A lot depends on
what they have to say. Okay?

1538
01:42:05.720 --> 01:42:08.041
YOUNG: Mmm.
I hear what you're saying, but...

1539
01:42:30.160 --> 01:42:31.571
You're here.

1540
01:42:34.000 --> 01:42:35.809
Yes, I'm here.

1541
01:42:41.480 --> 01:42:42.686
I'm glad.

1542
01:42:56.720 --> 01:42:58.688
Just in time.

1543
01:42:59.040 --> 01:43:01.407
In the matter of the <i>Southern
Christian Leadership Conference</i>

1544
01:43:01.480 --> 01:43:02.891
<i>v. the state of Alabama,</i>

1545
01:43:02.960 --> 01:43:06.521
I will now hear testimony
from the plaintiffs. Mr. Gray.

1546
01:43:07.680 --> 01:43:10.001
Your Honor, you will hear
testimony from the victims

1547
01:43:10.120 --> 01:43:12.805
who were beaten and bludgeoned
in their quest for freedom.

1548
01:43:13.760 --> 01:43:16.525
For their right to vote
and to self-determine.

1549
01:43:17.120 --> 01:43:18.246
The fact of the matter, Your Honor,

1550
01:43:18.320 --> 01:43:21.290
is that the incidents that occurred
cannot be disputed.

1551
01:43:21.720 --> 01:43:24.121
These particular circumstances

1552
01:43:24.640 --> 01:43:30.090
will paint a thorough picture
of the horrific events endured in Selma.

1553
01:43:30.760 --> 01:43:32.967
Very well, you may proceed.

1554
01:43:33.040 --> 01:43:37.170
Mr. King, you went out on that bridge
in direct violation of that judge's orders.

1555
01:43:37.880 --> 01:43:41.282
You deliberately disobeyed this judge
and the Governor, did you not?

1556
01:43:42.600 --> 01:43:45.729
Thousands of people came to Selma,

1557
01:43:45.800 --> 01:43:48.770
aroused by Sunday's brutal acts

1558
01:43:49.160 --> 01:43:52.846
exacted by officials of the city of Selma

1559
01:43:52.920 --> 01:43:54.763
and the state of Alabama.

1560
01:43:54.840 --> 01:43:57.889
I felt if I had not led the march,

1561
01:43:58.000 --> 01:44:00.002
pent-up emotions and inner tensions

1562
01:44:00.080 --> 01:44:04.369
would have led to an uncontrollable
retaliatory situation,

1563
01:44:05.760 --> 01:44:08.491
a violent situation on both sides.

1564
01:44:08.560 --> 01:44:10.130
I don't need any of your preaching
and prancing in here,

1565
01:44:10.200 --> 01:44:11.440
you hear? I want an answer.

1566
01:44:11.520 --> 01:44:12.806
Objection.

1567
01:44:12.880 --> 01:44:14.041
Watch it, counselor.

1568
01:44:14.560 --> 01:44:15.800
I'm trying very hard, Judge.

1569
01:44:16.160 --> 01:44:17.525
Try harder, counselor.

1570
01:44:23.200 --> 01:44:26.409
<i>It seems basic
to our constitutional principles</i>

1571
01:44:26.480 --> 01:44:29.689
<i>that the extent of the right to assemble,</i>

1572
01:44:30.480 --> 01:44:32.244
<i>and demonstrate and march</i>

1573
01:44:32.320 --> 01:44:34.368
<i>along the highway in a peaceful manner</i>

1574
01:44:34.440 --> 01:44:35.726
<i>ought to be commensurate</i>

1575
01:44:35.800 --> 01:44:38.326
<i>with the enormity of the wrongs</i>

1576
01:44:38.400 --> 01:44:40.721
<i>that are being protested
and petitioned against.</i>

1577
01:44:41.640 --> 01:44:46.168
<i>In this case, the wrongs are enormous.</i>

1578
01:44:48.640 --> 01:44:49.766
<i>Therefore,</i>

1579
01:44:50.760 --> 01:44:54.003
the extent of the right to demonstrate

1580
01:44:54.080 --> 01:44:57.562
in an estimated five-day march
from Selma to Montgomery

1581
01:44:58.240 --> 01:44:59.924
has been approved accordingly.

1582
01:45:00.360 --> 01:45:02.010
MAN: Yes!
WOMAN: Thank God!

1583
01:45:02.080 --> 01:45:03.923
(CROWD MURMURING)

1584
01:45:04.040 --> 01:45:06.327
JUDGE: There's no further
business with this court.

1585
01:45:06.840 --> 01:45:10.561
These proceedings are concluded,
with our thanks to the litigants.

1586
01:45:11.880 --> 01:45:13.689
Good day, gentlemen.

1587
01:45:24.720 --> 01:45:27.530
(INDISTINCT)

1588
01:45:29.120 --> 01:45:30.167
MAN: Yeah, that's right.

1589
01:45:30.240 --> 01:45:32.561
Well, now, we don't like
to have no mistakes, if you...

1590
01:45:32.680 --> 01:45:33.841
If you're sure about it.

1591
01:45:35.360 --> 01:45:39.001
Bayard says that Harry says
he can get Nina Simone,

1592
01:45:39.080 --> 01:45:43.210
Dick Gregory, Joan Baez,
Peter, Paul and Mary in.

1593
01:45:43.280 --> 01:45:44.406
(PEOPLE EXCLAIMING IN SURPRISE)

1594
01:45:44.480 --> 01:45:46.244
Come on now.
We don't got money for that.

1595
01:45:46.360 --> 01:45:48.362
Well, Harry is chartering a plane himself.

1596
01:45:48.440 --> 01:45:51.410
(SINGING) <i>Day-O, day-O</i>

1597
01:45:52.360 --> 01:45:56.206
ALL: <i>Daylight come
and me wan' go home</i>

1598
01:45:56.280 --> 01:46:01.650
President's angling for your blocking
of the march to be overturned.

1599
01:46:02.320 --> 01:46:04.846
Unfortunately, all my maneuvers
have been put on hold

1600
01:46:04.960 --> 01:46:07.201
while the matter's being adjudicated.

1601
01:46:16.360 --> 01:46:17.646
JOHNSON: <i>Governor,
you wanted to talk.</i>

1602
01:46:18.600 --> 01:46:20.284
Well, Mr. President...

1603
01:46:21.400 --> 01:46:23.846
Malcontents are disrupting Alabama,

1604
01:46:23.920 --> 01:46:27.208
and it's your responsibility to stop them.

1605
01:46:28.000 --> 01:46:30.685
They're protesting about the right to vote

1606
01:46:30.760 --> 01:46:34.082
and the way they're treated in your state.

1607
01:46:34.200 --> 01:46:38.410
So that's your problem,
your responsibility,

1608
01:46:38.480 --> 01:46:40.482
and it's on your watch.

1609
01:46:41.120 --> 01:46:43.168
Mr. President, I disagree.

1610
01:46:43.800 --> 01:46:47.202
We have a certain way things are done.
It's the way it is.

1611
01:46:47.280 --> 01:46:49.487
And it's the way
the people want it to stay.

1612
01:46:51.640 --> 01:46:53.927
George, why are you doing this?

1613
01:46:54.000 --> 01:46:55.889
Your whole career
has been working for the poor.

1614
01:46:55.960 --> 01:46:57.644
Why are you off on this black thing?

1615
01:46:58.160 --> 01:47:00.811
Well, 'cause you can't ever satisfy them.

1616
01:47:01.880 --> 01:47:03.769
First, it's the front seat of the bus.

1617
01:47:03.840 --> 01:47:06.491
Next, it's take over the parks,

1618
01:47:06.560 --> 01:47:08.289
then it's the public schools,

1619
01:47:08.400 --> 01:47:11.085
then it's voting, then it's jobs,

1620
01:47:11.160 --> 01:47:14.323
then it's distribution
of wealth without work.

1621
01:47:17.000 --> 01:47:18.923
George, you seen
all those demonstrators

1622
01:47:19.000 --> 01:47:20.286
out front of the White House

1623
01:47:20.360 --> 01:47:22.567
keeping my Lady Bird awake
the whole damn night?

1624
01:47:22.640 --> 01:47:24.608
Oh, yes, Mr. President. I saw them.

1625
01:47:24.680 --> 01:47:27.570
Well, let's go out there, you and I,

1626
01:47:27.640 --> 01:47:31.042
and announce that you've decided
to let the blacks vote undeterred,

1627
01:47:31.720 --> 01:47:33.449
and this whole mess will go away.

1628
01:47:33.520 --> 01:47:36.524
And I don't have to draft bills
or force the issue.

1629
01:47:37.720 --> 01:47:39.802
Now, why don't we do that, George?

1630
01:47:39.880 --> 01:47:42.724
Why don't you just let the niggers vote?

1631
01:47:43.560 --> 01:47:45.688
You agree they got the right to vote,
don't you?

1632
01:47:45.760 --> 01:47:47.603
Oh, there's no quarrel with that.

1633
01:47:47.680 --> 01:47:49.762
I know that. That's the law.

1634
01:47:50.720 --> 01:47:52.529
Then why don't you just let 'em vote?

1635
01:47:52.920 --> 01:47:54.490
I don't have that power.

1636
01:47:54.560 --> 01:47:56.449
It belongs to the county registrars.

1637
01:47:56.520 --> 01:47:58.727
Now, don't shit me
about who runs Alabama.

1638
01:48:00.040 --> 01:48:04.523
I don't have any legal power
over the county registrars, Mr. President.

1639
01:48:04.600 --> 01:48:06.728
They have their regulations
and they adhere.

1640
01:48:07.400 --> 01:48:09.687
Are you trying to shit me,
George Wallace?

1641
01:48:10.240 --> 01:48:12.527
Are you trying
to fuck over your President?

1642
01:48:12.600 --> 01:48:13.761
Mr. President...

1643
01:48:13.880 --> 01:48:16.121
We shouldn't even
be thinking about 1965.

1644
01:48:16.200 --> 01:48:18.931
We should be thinking about 1985.

1645
01:48:19.600 --> 01:48:21.762
You and I'll be both dead
and gone by then.

1646
01:48:23.040 --> 01:48:25.168
In 1985, what do you want looking back?

1647
01:48:25.240 --> 01:48:27.004
You want people
remembering you sayin',

1648
01:48:27.080 --> 01:48:31.483
"Wait," or "I can't,"
or, uh, "It's too hard"?

1649
01:48:34.400 --> 01:48:36.846
I don't right care what they think,

1650
01:48:36.920 --> 01:48:39.321
and you shouldn't neither.

1651
01:48:44.720 --> 01:48:45.926
Well...

1652
01:48:47.320 --> 01:48:49.448
I'll be damned if I'm gonna let history

1653
01:48:49.520 --> 01:48:52.888
put me in the same place
as the likes of you.

1654
01:48:57.000 --> 01:49:00.561
<i>I speak tonight for the dignity of man</i>

1655
01:49:00.640 --> 01:49:03.769
<i>and the destiny of democracy.</i>

1656
01:49:04.640 --> 01:49:07.962
<i>At times, history and fate</i>

1657
01:49:08.040 --> 01:49:11.965
<i>meet at a single time in a single place.</i>

1658
01:49:13.160 --> 01:49:18.121
<i>So it was last week in Selma, Alabama.</i>

1659
01:49:19.400 --> 01:49:22.404
<i>There, long suffering men and women</i>

1660
01:49:22.800 --> 01:49:28.409
<i>peacefully protested the denial
of their rights as Americans.</i>

1661
01:49:28.480 --> 01:49:30.608
<i>Rarely in any time</i>

1662
01:49:30.680 --> 01:49:33.923
<i>does an issue lay bare the secret heart</i>

1663
01:49:34.880 --> 01:49:36.848
<i>of America itself.</i>

1664
01:49:37.840 --> 01:49:42.368
<i>The issue for equal rights
for the American Negro</i>

1665
01:49:42.440 --> 01:49:43.726
<i>is that issue.</i>

1666
01:49:45.000 --> 01:49:46.001
<i>For this issue,</i>

1667
01:49:47.000 --> 01:49:50.004
<i>many of them were brutally assaulted.</i>

1668
01:49:54.480 --> 01:49:58.565
<i>There is no Negro problem.
There is no Southern problem.</i>

1669
01:49:59.640 --> 01:50:02.689
<i>There is only an American problem.</i>

1670
01:50:02.840 --> 01:50:04.569
(POLITICIANS APPLAUDING)

1671
01:50:05.840 --> 01:50:12.291
<i>The Constitution says that
no person shall be kept from voting</i>

1672
01:50:12.360 --> 01:50:15.011
<i>because of his race or color.</i>

1673
01:50:16.240 --> 01:50:20.245
<i>To correct the denial
of this fundamental right,</i>

1674
01:50:20.320 --> 01:50:24.848
<i>this Wednesday,
I will send to Congress a law</i>

1675
01:50:24.920 --> 01:50:29.005
<i>designed to eliminate
these illegal barriers.</i>

1676
01:50:29.560 --> 01:50:35.806
<i>The bill will strike down
voting restrictions in all elections,</i>

1677
01:50:35.880 --> 01:50:39.601
<i>federal, state and local.</i>

1678
01:50:41.360 --> 01:50:43.328
<i>And we shall do this.</i>

1679
01:50:45.400 --> 01:50:48.722
<i>We shall overcome.</i>

1680
01:50:49.360 --> 01:50:51.249
(APPLAUSE)

1681
01:51:06.280 --> 01:51:08.442
We believe we can cover you
through Lowndes County,

1682
01:51:08.520 --> 01:51:12.161
but once we add the final day's march
through Montgomery,

1683
01:51:12.240 --> 01:51:14.846
and you're passing through
all those tall buildings and whatnot,

1684
01:51:14.920 --> 01:51:16.888
coverage becomes challenging.

1685
01:51:18.600 --> 01:51:20.967
So please consider

1686
01:51:22.120 --> 01:51:23.690
driving in on the final leg.

1687
01:51:23.760 --> 01:51:27.321
And please consider nixing
the speech at the Capitol.

1688
01:51:29.600 --> 01:51:31.728
Well, if Wallace
will see us when we arrive,

1689
01:51:31.800 --> 01:51:33.928
there'll be no need for a speech.

1690
01:51:34.440 --> 01:51:36.522
- (CHUCKLES)
- Can you arrange that?

1691
01:51:42.720 --> 01:51:44.131
I can't hide.

1692
01:51:45.560 --> 01:51:48.291
We can't hide. You understand.

1693
01:51:52.160 --> 01:51:54.811
I don't want to see this go wrong for you.

1694
01:51:57.240 --> 01:51:59.607
Don't you want
to protect yourself, Doctor?

1695
01:52:01.360 --> 01:52:03.488
Let me try to do that.

1696
01:52:05.960 --> 01:52:10.284
You know, I know you want to live to see
the fruits of all this work. I know you do.

1697
01:52:12.960 --> 01:52:16.362
I'm just asking you
to allow us to help you do that.

1698
01:52:24.480 --> 01:52:26.926
I'm no different than anybody else.

1699
01:52:29.000 --> 01:52:31.162
I want to live long and be happy.

1700
01:52:34.160 --> 01:52:37.209
But I'll not be focusing
on what I want today.

1701
01:52:39.000 --> 01:52:41.321
I'm focused on what God wants.

1702
01:52:44.680 --> 01:52:49.129
We're here for a reason,
through many, many storms.

1703
01:52:53.480 --> 01:52:55.448
But, today, the sun is shining,

1704
01:52:55.520 --> 01:52:57.363
and I'm about to stand in its warmth

1705
01:52:57.440 --> 01:53:01.684
alongside a lot of freedom-loving people
who worked hard to get us here.

1706
01:53:03.120 --> 01:53:07.205
I may not be with them
for all the sunny days to come,

1707
01:53:09.160 --> 01:53:11.925
but as long as there
is light ahead for them,

1708
01:53:14.200 --> 01:53:16.089
it's worth it to me.

1709
01:53:25.520 --> 01:53:27.170
Thank you, John.

1710
01:53:28.120 --> 01:53:31.488
(FOLK MUSIC PLAYING)

1711
01:53:37.720 --> 01:53:40.371
(INAUDIBLE)

1712
01:55:10.160 --> 01:55:11.321
(CROWD CHEERING)

1713
01:55:11.400 --> 01:55:15.007
KING: <i>We heard them say
we'd never make it here.</i>

1714
01:55:17.280 --> 01:55:21.842
<i>We heard them say they'd stop us,
if it was the last thing they did.</i>

1715
01:55:23.840 --> 01:55:27.845
<i>We heard them say
we don't deserve to be here.</i>

1716
01:55:29.840 --> 01:55:33.890
<i>But today, we stand as Americans.</i>

1717
01:55:35.000 --> 01:55:36.729
(CROWD CHEERING)

1718
01:55:37.640 --> 01:55:39.210
<i>We are here,</i>

1719
01:55:40.040 --> 01:55:43.249
<i>and we ain't gonna let nobody
turn us around.</i>

1720
01:55:44.680 --> 01:55:47.206
<i>This mighty march,</i>

1721
01:55:48.040 --> 01:55:50.327
<i>which will be counted
as one of the greatest</i>

1722
01:55:50.400 --> 01:55:54.246
<i>demonstrations of protest and progress,</i>

1723
01:55:54.320 --> 01:55:57.608
<i>ends here in the Capitol of Alabama</i>

1724
01:55:57.720 --> 01:55:59.768
<i>for a vital purpose.</i>

1725
01:56:00.680 --> 01:56:04.924
<i>We have not fought only
for the right to sit where we please</i>

1726
01:56:05.000 --> 01:56:08.129
<i>and go to school where we please.</i>

1727
01:56:08.200 --> 01:56:12.410
<i>We do not only strive here today
to vote as we please.</i>

1728
01:56:13.520 --> 01:56:15.284
<i>But with our commitment,</i>

1729
01:56:15.360 --> 01:56:19.524
<i>we give birth each day to a new energy</i>

1730
01:56:19.600 --> 01:56:23.161
<i>that is stronger than
our strongest opposition.</i>

1731
01:56:23.240 --> 01:56:25.288
(CROWD CHEERING)

1732
01:56:25.360 --> 01:56:28.728
<i>And we embrace
this new energy so boldly,</i>

1733
01:56:28.800 --> 01:56:31.246
<i>embody it so fervently,</i>

1734
01:56:31.320 --> 01:56:34.483
<i>that its reflection illuminates
a great darkness.</i>

1735
01:56:34.960 --> 01:56:36.291
(CHEERING)

1736
01:56:37.400 --> 01:56:40.609
<i>Our society has distorted who we are.</i>

1737
01:56:41.840 --> 01:56:44.491
<i>From slavery to the Reconstruction</i>

1738
01:56:44.600 --> 01:56:48.321
<i>to the precipice at which we now stand,</i>

1739
01:56:48.400 --> 01:56:53.930
<i>we have seen powerful
white men rule the world</i>

1740
01:56:54.600 --> 01:56:59.481
<i>while offering poor white men
a vicious lie as placation.</i>

1741
01:57:00.560 --> 01:57:03.484
<i>And when the poor white man's children</i>

1742
01:57:03.560 --> 01:57:07.042
<i>wail with a hunger
that cannot be satisfied,</i>

1743
01:57:07.640 --> 01:57:11.247
<i>he feeds them that same vicious lie.</i>

1744
01:57:11.600 --> 01:57:12.965
(CROWD AGREEING)

1745
01:57:13.040 --> 01:57:14.485
<i>A lie whispering to them</i>

1746
01:57:15.280 --> 01:57:17.601
<i>that regardless of their lot in life,</i>

1747
01:57:18.400 --> 01:57:22.086
<i>they can at least be
triumphant in the knowledge</i>

1748
01:57:22.160 --> 01:57:26.961
<i>that their whiteness makes them
superior to blackness.</i>

1749
01:57:27.440 --> 01:57:28.965
<i>But we know the truth.</i>

1750
01:57:30.320 --> 01:57:35.486
<i>We know the truth, and we will
go forward to that truth, to freedom.</i>

1751
01:57:35.960 --> 01:57:37.325
(CHEERING)

1752
01:57:38.640 --> 01:57:40.529
<i>We will not be stopped.</i>

1753
01:57:42.280 --> 01:57:44.282
<i>We will march for our rights.</i>

1754
01:57:44.360 --> 01:57:48.331
<i>We will march to demand
treatment as full citizens.</i>

1755
01:57:48.760 --> 01:57:52.242
<i>We will march until the viciousness
and the darkness</i>

1756
01:57:52.320 --> 01:57:55.210
<i>gives way to the light of righteousness.</i>

1757
01:57:55.280 --> 01:57:56.361
(CHEERING)

1758
01:57:56.440 --> 01:58:00.047
<i>No man, no myth,</i>

1759
01:58:00.640 --> 01:58:04.964
<i>no malaise will stop this movement.</i>

1760
01:58:05.040 --> 01:58:09.762
<i>We forbid it. For we know
that it is this darkness</i>

1761
01:58:09.840 --> 01:58:14.164
<i>that murders the best in us
and the best of us.</i>

1762
01:58:15.320 --> 01:58:19.120
<i>Whether Jimmie Lee Jackson
or James Reeb,</i>

1763
01:58:21.000 --> 01:58:24.288
<i>or four blameless little girls</i>

1764
01:58:24.560 --> 01:58:29.248
<i>struck down
before they had even begun.</i>

1765
01:58:30.520 --> 01:58:35.287
<i>You may ask, when will we
be free of this darkness?</i>

1766
01:58:35.360 --> 01:58:37.886
<i>I say to you today,
my brothers and sisters,</i>

1767
01:58:38.320 --> 01:58:41.642
<i>despite the pain, despite the tears,</i>

1768
01:58:41.760 --> 01:58:44.525
<i>our freedom will soon be upon us.</i>

1769
01:58:44.600 --> 01:58:47.001
(CROWD CHEERING)

1770
01:58:47.080 --> 01:58:51.722
<i>For "truth crushed to earth
will rise again."</i>

1771
01:58:54.200 --> 01:58:56.601
<i>When will we be free?</i>

1772
01:58:57.560 --> 01:58:59.927
<i>Soon, and very soon.</i>

1773
01:59:00.000 --> 01:59:02.970
<i>Because you shall reap what you sow.</i>

1774
01:59:07.080 --> 01:59:08.889
<i>When will we be free?</i>

1775
01:59:09.560 --> 01:59:11.847
<i>Soon, and very soon.</i>

1776
01:59:12.560 --> 01:59:15.882
<i>Because no lie can live forever.</i>

1777
01:59:19.120 --> 01:59:21.521
<i>When will we be free?</i>

1778
01:59:21.600 --> 01:59:23.568
<i>Soon, and very soon</i>

1779
01:59:23.640 --> 01:59:29.204
<i>because "Mine eyes have seen
the glory of the coming of the Lord.</i>

1780
01:59:29.280 --> 01:59:33.888
<i>"He is trampling out the vintage
where the grapes of wrath are stored.</i>

1781
01:59:33.960 --> 01:59:38.170
<i>"He hath loosed the fateful lightning
of his terrible swift sword.</i>

1782
01:59:38.240 --> 01:59:40.368
<i>"His truth is marching on.</i>

1783
01:59:40.440 --> 01:59:46.971
<i>"Glory! Hallelujah!</i>

1784
01:59:47.040 --> 01:59:50.283
<i>"His truth is marching on."</i>

1785
01:59:54.320 --> 01:59:57.290
(INSPIRATIONAL SONG PLAYING)

1786
02:04:22.640 --> 02:04:25.883
(WORKERS IN SELMA SINGING
TRADITIONAL HYMNS)
